  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 1, 'Catch one unhelpful thought today and write it down word for word.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 2, 'Take a thought that upset you and ask: what is the evidence for it, and what is the evidence against it?'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 3, 'Notice one "always" or "never" in your thinking today and swap it for "sometimes."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 4, 'When a thought says the worst will happen, write down the most likely outcome next to it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 5, 'Ask yourself what you would say to a friend who had the thought you just had. Say that to yourself.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 6, 'Notice one time today you assumed you knew what someone else was thinking. Write down two other possibilities.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 7, 'Turn one "I should" into "I could" or "I would like to" and see how it changes the pressure.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 8, 'Rate a thought''s power from zero to ten now, then again in an hour. Notice whether it moved.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 9, 'Catch a thought that blames you for everything and list two other factors that played a part.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 10, 'Write an unhelpful thought on a sticky note, then write a fairer version underneath it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 11, 'When you notice a harsh label like "lazy" or "stupid," replace it with a description of what actually happened.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 12, 'Ask one thought: "Is this a fact or a feeling?" Sort it into the right pile.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 13, 'Take a thought that feels certain and add the words "I am having the thought that" in front of it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 14, 'Spot one prediction you made today and check later whether it came true.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 15, 'Write down a thought that ignores the good parts, then add the parts it left out.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 16, 'Notice a thought that starts with "what if" and answer it with "then I would."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 17, 'Give a repeating thought a silly voice in your head and hear how it sounds.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 18, 'Pick one thought that is not helping and ask: "Will this matter in a month?"'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 19, 'Write down the thought you have most often about yourself and one piece of evidence that does not fit it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 20, 'When you catch yourself mind-reading, ask the person directly instead, if you can.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 21, 'Take a thought about the future and list one thing that is within your control today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 22, 'Notice a thought that compares you to someone else and write down what you are comparing against, their highlight reel or their whole life.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 23, 'Write down one thought that you have been treating as an order, then ask whether you agree with it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 24, 'Spend two minutes listing three explanations for something that went wrong today, not just the one that blames you.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 25, 'Rewrite one all-or-nothing thought on a scale from zero to one hundred.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 26, 'Notice a thought that predicts embarrassment and write down what would actually happen if it came true.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 27, 'Catch a "here we go again" thought and write down one way today is different from last time.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 28, 'Ask a recurring thought: "What would I need to know to let this go?" and go find it, if you can.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 29, 'Write a thought that says you cannot cope, then list three hard things you have already gotten through.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 30, 'Review your notes from this challenge and circle the thinking pattern that showed up most. Name it so you can spot it faster.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 31, 'Set a timer for five minutes and write every thought that runs through your head. Then underline the ones that were not helping.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 32, 'Pick a thought that jumps to the worst case and write the best case beside it, then the middle case. Circle the one that seems most likely.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 33, 'Before a meeting or appointment today, write down what you predict will happen. Afterward, note what actually happened.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 34, 'Notice a thought that uses the word "everyone" or "nobody" and count how many people you actually mean.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 35, 'When a thought says you failed, write down what percentage of the task actually went wrong.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 36, 'Draw two columns on a page: "what the thought says" and "what I would tell a coworker in the same spot." Fill both.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 37, 'Catch a thought that skips straight to a conclusion and write down the steps it left out.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 38, 'On your commute or walk today, notice one thought that talked you down and answer it out loud in your head.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 39, 'Ask a thought that feels urgent: "What is the rush?" Write the answer down.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 40, 'Take a thought about a mistake and ask whether you would still remember it a year from now.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 41, 'Notice a thought that says "I can''t" and rewrite it as "I haven''t yet" or "I don''t want to." See which is closer to the truth.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 42, 'Find one thought today that treats a possibility as a certainty and add the word "might" to it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 43, 'Write a thought that assumes the worst about someone''s silence, then list three ordinary reasons a person goes quiet.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 44, 'Choose a thought that keeps circling and give it a name, like "the Sunday loop." Say the name when it shows up.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 45, 'Before bed, write down one unhelpful thought from the day and one thing it got wrong.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 46, 'When you catch a thought that discounts a compliment, write the compliment down as if it were true.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 47, 'Ask a "what if" thought how many times its prediction has come true in the past. Write the number down.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 48, 'Pick a thought that says a small setback ruins the whole day, then list what is still fine.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 49, 'Hear a thought that begins "they must think" and finish the sentence with "or they might not be thinking about me at all."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 50, 'Take one thought that feels like a fact and try to say it as an opinion instead, starting with "in my view."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 51, 'Write down a thought that makes a whole judgment from one event, then find one event that points the other way.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 52, 'Spot a thought that uses "should" about someone else today and rewrite it as a preference.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 53, 'Keep a tally on paper of how many times one specific thought shows up today. Note when it was loudest.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 54, 'Catch a thought that says you are behind and write down who set the schedule you are measuring yourself against.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 55, 'Notice a thought that treats a feeling as proof, like "I feel awkward so I must have been awkward," and separate the two.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 56, 'When a thought predicts rejection, write the two most likely responses you would actually get instead.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 57, 'Rewrite an unhelpful thought as a question rather than a statement, then try to answer it honestly.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 58, 'Take a thought that says something will be a disaster and describe the disaster in detail. Then ask how survivable it really is.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 59, 'Notice a thought that decides an outcome before you have tried, and set a small experiment to test it this afternoon.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 60, 'Pick a thought that is loud at work and ask whether it would sound the same at home. Write down the difference.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 61, 'Write down one thought that assumes you are responsible for someone else''s mood, and list what is theirs to carry.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 62, 'Ask a repeating thought what it is trying to protect you from. Write the answer, then decide whether the protection is needed today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 63, 'Catch one "I always mess this up" and list the last three times you did not.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 64, 'Notice a thought that jumps from one bad email to a bad job to a bad life. Stop the chain at the first link and stay there.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 65, 'Write the harshest thought you had about yourself today, then rewrite it in the plain tone of a weather report.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 66, 'When a thought says you cannot ask for help, write down one person and one sentence you could use.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 67, 'Spot a thought that borrows trouble from tomorrow and write down what tomorrow actually needs from you today. Usually it is nothing.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 68, 'Take a thought that says you are the only one who struggles with this, and name one other person who probably does too.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 69, 'Look back on a worry from last month and write down whether the thing it predicted happened.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 70, 'Notice a thought that says "this is how it will always be" and write the last time something changed that you did not expect.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 71, 'Rate how much you believe an unhelpful thought before and after you write out the evidence. Note both numbers.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 72, 'Interrupt the thought that you are wasting time, then write down what you actually did in the last hour.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 73, 'Ask a thought that says "I have to" who is making you. Write down the honest answer.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 74, 'Pick a thought that grades you as a whole person from one moment, and regrade the moment alone.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 75, 'Turn one worried thought into a plan with one step, then do that step before dinner.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 76, 'Notice a thought that says someone is angry with you and write down the evidence, not the tone you imagined.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 77, 'Jot down a thought insisting you cannot change, then list one small thing you do differently now than five years ago.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 78, 'Catch a thought that ends with "so there''s no point" and add "unless" to the end. Finish the sentence.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 79, 'When you are waiting in line or on hold today, notice where your thoughts go and steer one of them somewhere more useful.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 80, 'Take a thought that magnifies a flaw and ask whether you would even notice it in someone else.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 81, 'Ask a thought that predicts the worst: "And then what?" Keep asking until the answer is something you could handle.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 82, 'Write down a thought that says a good thing was luck, then note one part of it that came from your effort.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 83, 'Notice one thought today that argued against resting and write down whether the argument held up.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 84, 'Spot the thought that says you must get it right the first time, and write down what a second try would cost.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 85, 'Choose one thought that has been running for days and write it a short reply, as if answering a persistent email.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 86, 'Catch a thought that reads a whole relationship from one short text, and write what else you know about that person.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 87, 'Question a thought that says you are not good enough and ask: good enough for what, and by whose measure?'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 88, 'Write down a thought that compares this year to a better year, then list two things you have now that you did not have then.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 89, 'Notice a thought that says you are too old or too late for something, and name one person who started later.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 90, 'Practice one calm sentence you can say to yourself when a thought spirals, like "That''s the loop, not the truth." Use it once today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 91, 'Pick an unhelpful thought and write what a kind but honest mentor would say about it in two sentences.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 92, 'Sort three thoughts from today into "solvable" and "not mine to solve." Act on one from the first pile.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 93, 'When a thought says a conversation went badly, write down one line from it that actually went fine.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 94, 'Notice a thought that treats being unsure as proof that something is wrong. Write down what being unsure actually means.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 95, 'Hold a thought that says you have to decide right now, and write down what would change if you decided tomorrow instead.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 96, 'Catch a thought that turns a preference into a rule, like "I must never be late," and rewrite it with "I prefer."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 97, 'Write a thought that predicts you will freeze in a moment, then write the smallest thing you could do if you did.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 98, 'Ask a thought that puts you down whether it uses words you would never use about a friend. Replace them.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 99, 'Look at one thought from a distance, as if it were on a screen across the room, and describe it in three words.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 100, 'Notice a thought that keeps replaying an old conversation, and write down what you would do differently rather than what went wrong.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 101, 'Over lunch today, notice one thought about how the afternoon will go and check it against how the afternoon actually goes.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 102, 'Write down a thought that assumes a delay means bad news, then list two neutral reasons things take longer.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 103, 'Describe a moment you think you handled badly and describe what you did in plain, factual sentences with no adjectives.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 104, 'Ask a thought that calls something "unbearable" whether you are, in fact, bearing it right now.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 105, 'Pick a thought about a person who annoyed you today and write one thing that might be going on in their day.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 106, 'When a thought says "I knew this would happen," check whether you also predicted the times it did not.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 107, 'Notice one thought today that treated a maybe as a no. Write down what a maybe actually leaves open.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 108, 'Take an unhelpful thought and write it in the third person, using your name, then read it back.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 109, 'Spot a thought that says everyone is judging you in a store, at the gym or on the street, and count how many people actually looked your way.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 110, 'Time-check a thought that says a task will take forever, then time how long the first ten minutes really take.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 111, 'Catch yourself replaying a mistake from years ago and write down one thing you learned from it that you still use.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 112, 'Ask one nagging thought: "If a coworker said this to me, would I believe them?" Write your answer.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 113, 'Notice a thought that treats one quiet reply as a verdict on you, and write down what the person may have been busy with.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 114, 'List the people a thought says you are letting down and name the specific people. Then ask each one, in your head, whether they agree.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 115, 'When a thought insists on a perfect result, write down what "good enough to move on" would look like today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 116, 'Rewrite a thought that says "this is too hard" as "this is hard and here is my first step."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 117, 'Challenge the idea that you should already know how to do something, and write down when you would have learned it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 118, 'Notice one thought that turned a small ache or tired feeling into a serious story, and write down the ordinary explanation.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 119, 'Pick one thought from your morning and ask whether it was a plan or a threat. Rewrite the threat as a plan.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 120, 'While doing dishes or laundry tonight, listen for one repeated thought and answer it with one sentence of evidence.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 121, 'Unpack a thought that assumes someone''s success means your failure, then list how both could be true at once.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 122, 'Press a thought that says "I can''t handle this" on what "handle" would actually look like. Often it is smaller than it sounds.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 123, 'Spot a thought that uses "ruined" and rate the real damage from zero to ten.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 124, 'Notice when you explain a good day as a fluke and a bad day as the pattern. Try swapping the explanations once.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 125, 'Take a thought that says "I have no idea what I''m doing" and list three things you did today that show otherwise.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 126, 'Before you reply to a message that worried you, write down the story your thoughts built from it and the plain facts of what it said.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 127, 'Catch a thought that turns "I made a mistake" into "I am a mistake." Cross out the second version.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 128, 'Write down one thought that predicts boredom, dread or disappointment about an event, then attend it and grade the prediction.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 129, 'Ask a thought that keeps you from starting: "What is the worst that happens in the first minute?" Then start.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 130, 'Find a thought that treats a rule you made up as a law of nature. Write down who could change the rule.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 131, 'When a thought says you are too much, write down who told you that and whether you still trust their judgment.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 132, 'Look for a thought today that argues in circles, and write down its first sentence and its last. Notice they are the same.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 133, 'Pick a thought that fears a question you might be asked, and write out a two-sentence answer you would be fine giving.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 134, 'Answer a thought about being unprepared: and list what you have already done to prepare.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 135, 'Write a note to a thought that visits at three in the morning, and read it the next time it comes.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 136, 'Catch a thought that says the silence in a room is about you, and name two other things it could be about.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 137, 'Ask a self-critical thought to show its work. Write down the actual evidence it has, in a list.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 138, 'Notice a thought that jumps to what a family member will say, and write down what they have actually said in the past.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 139, 'Rewrite one dramatic thought in the flattest language you can manage, as if reading it from a manual.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 140, 'Audit a thought that says you wasted a whole weekend and list what the weekend actually contained, hour by hour if needed.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 141, 'If a thought says you are not a "math person" or "people person," write down one time you did the thing anyway.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 142, 'Spot a thought that expects you to read the future, and write down what you would need to know that you do not.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 143, 'Write down a thought that treats a bad first draft as proof of a bad writer, then write a second sentence of the draft.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 144, 'Notice a compliment turning into pressure in your head, like "now they''ll expect that every time," and write what was actually said.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 145, 'Notice one thought today that wanted to cancel a plan out of dread, and write down how you usually feel afterward when you go.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 146, 'Push a thought that says "I''m behind everyone" on who exactly is in that "everyone." Name three people and check.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 147, 'Pick a thought that has been telling you a coworker dislikes you and write down what a neutral observer would see.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 148, 'Take one worry about money and separate the part that is a fact from the part that is a forecast.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 149, 'Write down the thought that comes up when you look in the mirror, then write what you would say about a friend''s face.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 150, 'Separate being tired from being incapable when a thought blends them, and write down what tired people can still do.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 151, 'When a thought says "I''ll never learn this," write down the last skill you thought that about and now have.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 152, 'Catch a thought that reads disappointment into a short reply, then reread the reply looking only for its words.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 153, 'Ask a thought that predicts embarrassment in front of a group how many people will remember by next week.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 154, 'Spot a thought that says the day is wasted because the morning went sideways, and write down what the afternoon can still hold.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 155, 'Question a thought that treats your mood as a forecast for the whole week, then note how moods have shifted in the past.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 156, 'Meet a thought that says you are a burden and list what you have given someone recently, however small.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 157, 'Stop at a thought that says "this proves it" and ask what "it" is. Write the claim out in full and check it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 158, 'Pick one recurring thought and write down what it would need to see to change its mind. Then check whether that thing is already true.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 159, 'When a thought says someone is going to leave, write down the actual things they have done this week.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 160, 'Catch a thought that predicts a hard conversation going wrong, and write the first sentence you would actually say.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 161, 'Ask a thought that says you are wasting your life what one useful thing you could do in the next twenty minutes. Do it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 162, 'Write down a thought that measures your worth by your productivity, and list two things you value that have nothing to do with output.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 163, 'Notice a thought that assumes the worst about a doctor''s, teacher''s or boss''s request to talk, and list three routine reasons for the request.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 164, 'Examine a thought that says "I''m not ready" and write down what "ready" would look like. Check whether anyone is ever that ready.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 165, 'Rewrite a thought that begins "I bet they" as "I don''t actually know whether they."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 166, 'Spot one thought that wanted you to apologize for something that was not yours, and write down what was actually yours.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 167, 'Catch a thought that says today has to fix everything, and write down what today only needs to move a little.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 168, 'Ask a self-doubting thought: "Would I hire someone who thought this about themselves?" Write why or why not.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 169, 'Notice a thought that turns waiting for news into certainty about bad news, and write down the range of things the news could be.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 170, 'Record a thought that says you cannot say no, then list one small no you have said and survived.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 171, 'On a crisp fall morning, take a thought outside with you and see whether it sounds as convincing in daylight and cold air.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 172, 'This morning, write down a thought that says you cannot trust yourself, then list three decisions you made this year that turned out fine.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 173, 'Catch a "they''re only being polite" thought and write down what the person would have said if they were not being polite.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 174, 'Ask the thought that says you are failing as a parent, partner or friend what "passing" would actually look like. Be specific.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 175, 'Tonight, notice a thought that treats a full inbox as proof you are drowning, then count how many messages actually need you today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 176, 'Pick the meanest word a thought used about you today and look up its definition. Check whether it truly applies.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 177, 'When a thought predicts you will say something foolish at dinner, write down what you said last time and how many people cared.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 178, 'Turn one "why do I always" into "what happened this time" and answer only that.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 179, 'Take a thought about a coworker''s tone in an email and read the email aloud in a friendly voice. Notice whether the meaning holds.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 180, 'At your desk, rewrite a thought that begins "I''m the kind of person who" as "Today I did," and see how much smaller it gets.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 181, 'Spot a thought that argues you should have seen something coming, and write down what information you actually had at the time.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 182, 'Notice a thought that says one gray day means a gray season, and write down something you enjoyed the last time the weather turned.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 183, 'On the way home, write down a thought that assumes your partner or roommate is upset with you, then ask them one plain question about their day.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 184, 'Catch a thought that hands you a whole future of failure from one rejection, and write down what the rejection actually said.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 185, 'Over coffee, ask a thought that says "I''ll look stupid" to name who will be looking and for how long. Write the answers down.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 186, 'Take a thought that magnifies one awkward pause and write down how long the pause probably lasted in seconds.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 187, 'Notice when a thought tells you the story of what will happen before you arrive somewhere. Arrive, then compare.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 188, 'Pick one thought that keeps score against you and write the score fairly, with points for what went right.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 189, 'When a thought says you have let yourself down, write down what standard you were using and whether you chose it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 190, 'Write a thought that says a hard week means a hard life, then list two weeks this year that were easier.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 191, 'Catch a thought that uses "obviously," and check whether the thing is obvious to anyone but the thought.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 192, 'Ask a thought that predicts disaster at a family gathering what happened at the last three gatherings. Rate each one honestly.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 193, 'Spot one thought that reads a busy friend as a lost friend, and write down the last time they reached out to you.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 194, 'During a break, notice a thought that says you are not doing enough and write down what "enough" would look like today. Then check whether it is a moving target.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 195, 'Before you sleep, take a thought that says you are boring and write down one thing you talked about this week that someone found interesting.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 196, 'Give an unhelpful thought a job title, like "the forecaster" or "the judge," and note what it is not qualified for.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 197, 'Rewrite a thought that says "I have to be perfect at this" as "I have to be present for this."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 198, 'When you are stuck in traffic or a long line, catch one thought that spirals and write down its first false step when you get where you are going.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 199, 'Write down one thought that says a small change makes no difference, then name one small change that did.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 200, 'On a walk, catch a thought that turns a raised eyebrow into a verdict, and list three things an eyebrow can mean.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 201, 'Ask a thought that says nobody would understand who you have not yet tried telling.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 202, 'While cooking, notice a thought that says you cannot enjoy a summer evening because of a task waiting inside. Do the evening, then note whether the task got worse.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 203, 'Pick a thought that treats a checkup, review or grade as a test of your whole worth, and write down what it actually measures.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 204, 'Take a thought that expects a friend to be angry, and write the friendliest reading of their last message.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 205, 'Spot a thought that ends with "and that''s just how I am." Write one time you acted differently.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 206, 'When a thought says your idea is stupid, write the idea down anyway and rate it from zero to ten tomorrow.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 207, 'After work, write a thought that assumes the worst about a slow reply to a job application, then list three reasons hiring takes time.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 208, 'Catch a thought that says a rainy day is a ruined day and write down what the rain makes easier.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 209, 'At lunch, notice a thought that treats a compliment as a lie, and write down why someone would bother lying about that.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 210, 'Ask a thought that insists you must keep worrying whether the worrying has changed one outcome this month. Write the answer.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 211, 'Take a thought that says a holiday will go badly and write down one moment you could make go well.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 212, 'Pick a thought that says you are the problem in a group, and list two other factors the group faces.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 213, 'Rewrite an "I can''t stand it" thought as "I don''t like it," and notice whether the pressure drops.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 214, 'Notice when a thought says "this is a sign" and write down what else the same event could be a sign of, or whether it is a sign at all.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 215, 'Somewhere quiet, write down a thought that assumes everyone else is confident, then look around a room and count who looks unsure.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 216, 'In a waiting room, catch a thought that says you missed your chance and name one similar chance that is still open.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 217, 'Spot a thought that gives you the blame for weather, traffic or someone else''s mood, and hand the blame back.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 218, 'Ask a thought that says a long winter will be miserable what one thing you could look forward to in it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 219, 'First thing, take a thought that says you talk too much and write down whether anyone actually asked you to stop.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 220, 'Notice a thought that keeps you rereading a message you sent, and write down the worst the message could have done. Usually nothing.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 221, 'When a thought says you should have handled a loss better, write down what "better" means and who decides.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 222, 'Write down one thought that took a neutral fact, like a closed door, and gave it a story. Then write the plain fact alone.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 223, 'Midafternoon, catch a thought that says the whole project is doomed because one part slipped, and write down the parts still on track.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 224, 'In the car, pick a thought that treats a colleague''s promotion as your failure, and list what their promotion says about you. Probably nothing.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 225, 'Ask a thought that predicts a bad night''s sleep to write down what you will do tomorrow anyway. Then do it either way.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 226, 'On the bus or train, take a thought that says you are not creative and write down one thing you made, fixed or improvised this month.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 227, 'With a pen handy, notice a thought that says you have to answer immediately, and give yourself an hour before replying.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 228, 'Once today, rewrite a thought that says "I failed" as "I tried and it didn''t work this time."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 229, 'Spot a thought that calls a quiet weekend a lonely weekend, and list two things you chose to do alone and enjoyed.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 230, 'After dinner, write a thought that says you should feel better by now, and write down who set that deadline.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 231, 'If a thought predicts you will freeze in a job interview, sit down and write out your answer to the first likely question.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 232, 'On a slow Sunday, catch a thought that says you will regret a decision and write down what you would also regret if you did not make it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 233, 'Between tasks, ask a thought that says you are not a good friend to name three things a good friend does. Check them off honestly.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 234, 'Notice one thought that is a memory in disguise, like an old teacher''s voice, and write down whose voice it is.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 235, 'Take a thought that says spring cleaning proves how badly you have let things slide, and write down what the clutter actually is: stuff, not a verdict.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 236, 'Pick a thought that treats one sick day as falling apart, and list what a sick day is for.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 237, 'Write down one thought that insists a mistake will be talked about for years, then name a coworker''s mistake from last year. Can you?'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 238, 'In the checkout line, catch a thought that says a friend''s short "fine" means trouble, and write down what "fine" usually means from them.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 239, 'Ask a thought that reads a group text as excluding you what the group was actually talking about.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 240, 'Spot a thought that says you have nothing to add to a conversation, and write down one question you could ask instead.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 241, 'Before your first meeting, write down the thought you have while waiting for a text back, then set the phone down and give the thought a two-hour deadline to be proven.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 242, 'On your lunch break, catch a thought that says you are the worst at something and rank yourself honestly among people you actually know.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 243, 'Notice a thought that decides a party will be awkward, then write down one person there you will be glad to see.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 244, 'While the kettle boils, ask a thought that says "I''m too sensitive" whether the situation would bother most people. Write down your honest guess.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 245, 'As the day winds down, take a thought that says a late start ruins a morning, and write down what a late start actually cost: minutes, not the day.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 246, 'Pick a thought that turns a doctor''s routine question into a scary answer, and write down what routine questions are for.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 247, 'Should a thought insist you are not far enough along, write down where "along" leads and whether you even want to go there.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 248, 'Rewrite a thought that says "everyone is watching" as "a few people might glance," and check which one matches reality.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 249, 'Spot a thought that says a hot, tired afternoon proves you are lazy, and write down what heat does to everyone.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 250, 'Write a thought that assumes your manager''s silence means trouble, then list what managers are usually busy with.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 251, 'On the porch or balcony, catch a thought that says you are not allowed to be pleased with yourself, and write down one thing you did well this week.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 252, 'Notice a thought that expects a family dinner to end in an argument, and write down one topic you can steer toward instead.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 253, 'Right after waking, ask a thought that says you cannot afford a mistake what a mistake in this case would actually cost. Write the number or the consequence.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 254, 'Take a thought that reads a crowded room as a room full of critics, and pick one face that looks kind.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 255, 'Pick the thought that comes when you see a photo of yourself, and write down what a stranger would notice first. Probably not the thing you did.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 256, 'Halfway through the day, write down a thought that says your opinion does not count, then share the opinion once today anyway and see what happens.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 257, 'When a thought says a first cold morning of the year means months of misery, write down two things you like about cold mornings.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 258, 'When the house is quiet, catch a thought that reads a "we need to talk" as a catastrophe, and list three ordinary things people need to talk about.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 259, 'Notice a thought that argues you should not need help with something, and write down who else needs help with it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 260, 'Between errands, ask a thought that says a chore has to be done perfectly what a done-but-imperfect version would look like. Do that version.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 261, 'Spot a thought that tells you a good mood cannot last, and write down what it would cost to enjoy it while it is here.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 262, 'Take a thought that says an old friend''s silence means the friendship is over, and send them one line that asks nothing.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 263, 'With a notebook open, rewrite a thought that begins "I''ll probably fail" as "I''ll probably learn something," and check which is more often true.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 264, 'Write a thought that treats a compliment from your boss as a setup, then write the plain compliment on its own.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 265, 'Late in the afternoon, catch a thought that says you cannot start until you feel confident, and write down one thing you started without confidence.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 266, 'Before you check email, notice a thought that says you are wasting a beautiful day indoors, and write down what you are actually doing with it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 267, 'On a weekday evening, ask a thought that says "I''m such an idiot" what specifically happened, in one sentence with no insults.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 268, 'Pick a thought that assumes a group of laughing people is laughing at you, and write down what people usually laugh about.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 269, 'Each time a thought says you cannot trust a good result, write down what it would take to trust it. Then check whether you already have that.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 270, 'Take a thought that expects the worst from a vacation and write down one thing that could go right on the first day.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 271, 'Spot the thought that turns one forgotten name into "I''m losing it," and write down how many names you remembered today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 272, 'Write down a thought that tells you to give up on a habit after one missed day, then write what you would tell a friend who missed one.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 273, 'Whenever it shows up today, catch a thought that says a hard conversation last week means the relationship is broken, and list what has happened since.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 274, 'Notice a thought that keeps saying "if only," and rewrite it as "next time."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 275, 'This morning, ask a thought that says a stranger''s frown was about you where that stranger was probably going.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 276, 'Tonight, take a thought that says you are too quiet in meetings and write down one thing you said in a meeting that someone used.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 277, 'Pick one thought that treats a delay as a failure, and write down what the delay might make better.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 278, 'On the way home, rewrite a thought that says "I have to fix this now" as "I have to look at this now," and see whether the second one is enough.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 279, 'When a thought calls a whole year a failure, write down four things from it, one per season, that were not.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 280, 'Write a thought that says nobody noticed your work, then list one person who did and one way you could tell.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 281, 'Over coffee, catch a thought that says you are too far behind to catch up, and write down what "caught up" would mean by Friday.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 282, 'Before you sleep, notice a thought that decides a new coworker does not like you after one lunch, and write down what one lunch can tell you.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 283, 'On a walk, spot a thought that says the news means your own life is doomed, and write down what in your own day is still ordinary.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 284, 'While cooking, ask a thought that predicts a terrible commute whether the commute has ever been fine. Write down the ratio.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 285, 'After work, take a thought that says you ruined a gift, meal or plan, and write down the reaction the other person actually had.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 286, 'At lunch, pick a thought that says you need a sign before deciding, and write down what a sign could tell you that you do not already know.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 287, 'Somewhere quiet, write down the thought you have about a neighbor who did not wave, then wave first tomorrow and see what happens.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 288, 'The next time a thought says you should have known better, write down the age you were when the thing happened.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 289, 'First thing, catch a thought that says a quiet phone means nobody cares, and count the people you could call who would pick up.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 290, 'Midafternoon, notice a thought that treats a cluttered desk as a cluttered mind, and write down what the desk actually needs: ten minutes, not a diagnosis.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 291, 'In the car, ask a thought that says you cannot handle a summer of changes what you handled last summer. List two things.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 292, 'Take a thought that reads your own tiredness as failure, and write what a tired body is asking for.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 293, 'On the bus or train, rewrite a thought that says "I should be grateful, so I shouldn''t feel this" as "I can be grateful and still feel this."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 294, 'Spot a thought that fears a question at a holiday table, and write out a one-line answer you could give without explaining yourself.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 295, 'With a pen handy, write a thought that says a good review must be a mistake, then reread the review as if it were about someone else.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 296, 'Once today, catch a thought that says you will never be as good as your sibling, parent or mentor, and write down one thing you do that they do not.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 297, 'Notice a thought that argues against making a phone call, then make the call and grade the argument afterward.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 298, 'After dinner, ask a thought that says you cannot relax until everything is done when everything was last done. Write the date if you can.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 299, 'At the kitchen table, pick a thought that turns a missed workout, meal or plan into "I have no discipline," and write down one thing you do reliably every week.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 300, 'On a slow Sunday, take a thought that says a first date going badly means all dates will, and write down what a first date can actually tell you.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 301, 'When a thought says you look ridiculous in something, write down who you are dressing for and whether they would agree.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 302, 'Between tasks, write down a thought that says you should have spoken up sooner, then write down what you can say now, today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 303, 'At the end of the workday, catch a thought that reads a coworker leaving early as leaving you with the work, and check what they actually finished first.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 304, 'On your lunch break, notice a thought that treats a birthday as a scorecard, and write down two things the year gave you that were not on the card.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 305, 'While the kettle boils, spot a thought that says you are not allowed to change your mind, and write down who made that rule.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 306, 'Ask a thought that says the summer is slipping away what one thing you could still do with it this week. Plan it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 307, 'In a spare minute, take a thought that says you have to explain yourself and write down whether anyone actually asked.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 308, 'On the porch or balcony, rewrite a thought that says "I''m terrible at this" as "I''m new at this" or "I''m out of practice at this," whichever is true.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 309, 'Pick a thought that predicts you will cry in front of people, and write down what would actually happen if you did.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 310, 'Write a thought that says one tense phone call means a whole family is angry, and name the one person who was actually on the call.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 311, 'Keep a small card in your pocket with one question on it, "What else could be true?", and pull it out the next time a thought closes a door.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 312, 'Read yesterday''s unhelpful thought back today and note whether it still sounds as certain.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 313, 'Draw a quick pie chart of the blame for something that went wrong, and give honest slices to timing, other people and plain luck.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 314, 'Say an unhelpful thought slowly, one word at a time, and notice which word carries all the weight. Replace only that word.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 315, 'Count how many of your thoughts this hour were about the past, the future or right now. Steer one toward right now.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 316, 'Trade one "what will they think" for "what do I think," and write down your own answer first.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 317, 'Sit with a thought for sixty seconds without arguing or agreeing, then write down whether it got louder or quieter.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 318, 'Send yourself a short message with the fair version of a thought you had today, so it is waiting in your inbox tomorrow.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 319, 'Describe a recurring thought to a friend or partner in one sentence and ask them what they see in it that you might not.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 320, 'Underline every "must," "have to" and "need to" in something you wrote today, and decide which ones are actually true.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 321, 'Tell a thought that predicts the worst that it can have a turn later, then set a time this evening to hear it out on paper.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 322, 'Compare a thought''s confidence with its track record. Give it a grade for accuracy based on the last five times it showed up.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 323, 'Finish this sentence on paper: "The thought says X, but what I actually know is Y."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 324, 'Photograph something ordinary on your walk and write one thought you had about it that was pure interpretation.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 325, 'Listen for a thought that speaks in absolutes during a disagreement, and restate your point without the absolute.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 326, 'Test a thought that says you will be ignored by asking one small question in a group today and noting what happens.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 327, 'Choose a thought that you have been avoiding writing down because it feels too true, and write it anyway, then check it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 328, 'Let a thought that says "this is pointless" run to its end, then ask what you would do if it were only half right.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 329, 'Argue the opposite of an unhelpful thought for two minutes, as if you were paid to, and write down the strongest point you found.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 330, 'Watch for a thought that arrives with a tight jaw or a knot in your stomach, and write down which came first, the thought or the feeling.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 331, 'Reframe a thought about a slow, dark December evening as a description of what the evening is for, rather than what it lacks.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 332, 'Put a thought on trial for five minutes: prosecution, defense, verdict. Write the verdict in one line.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 333, 'Search one unhelpful thought for a hidden rule, like "people who ask for things are weak," and write the rule down so you can see it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 334, 'Repeat a thought that keeps predicting failure in a whisper, then in a bored voice, and notice which version you believe less.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 335, 'Track one thought across the day on a sticky note: when it came, how strong, what set it off. Look for the pattern at bedtime.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 336, 'Introduce a thought to a fact. Write the thought, then one number, date or quote that bears on it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 337, 'Set aside a thought about a spring deadline until you have written down the three next steps, then see whether the thought still needs airtime.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 338, 'Rehearse a fair response to your most common thought until you can say it without reading it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 339, 'Model the future the way a thought does, then the way a calm planner would. Write both timelines side by side.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 340, 'Point out to yourself, silently, when a thought is telling a story about someone''s motives, and add "or not" at the end.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 341, 'Turn a thought that hits at the end of a long summer day into a question you can answer tomorrow, and put it down for the night.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 342, 'Check whether a thought that feels new is actually one you have had before, and write down what changed the last time it passed.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 343, 'Replace "I am" with "I feel" in one thought today and see whether the sentence gets more honest.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 344, 'Explain to an imaginary ten-year-old why a thought you had today is not the whole story. Use small words.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 345, 'Stand in a doorway between rooms and leave one unhelpful thought behind in the room you are leaving, on purpose, to see whether it follows.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 346, 'Cross out one word in an unhelpful thought and see if the sentence still stands. Keep crossing until it falls over.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 347, 'Review three predictions you wrote down over the past weeks and give your inner forecaster a batting average.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 348, 'Plan the fair answer to a thought you know will come during a holiday visit, and carry it with you.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 349, 'Question a thought that shows up every year when the clocks change, and write down what it gets wrong about the darker afternoons.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 350, 'Match a thought to the thinking pattern it belongs to, like all-or-nothing, mind-reading or fortune-telling, and write the pattern''s name next to it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 351, 'Decide in advance how you will answer "I''m not good at this" the next time it comes up in the kitchen, at the gym or at your desk.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 352, 'Thank a thought for trying to keep you safe, then tell it you will take it from here. Write down what "taking it from here" means today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 353, 'Interrupt a chain of thoughts by writing down only the second link and asking whether it follows from the first.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 354, 'Recall one time a thought told you not to try and you tried anyway. Write down what the thought missed.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 355, 'Grade an unhelpful thought on a report card: accuracy, usefulness, fairness. Give a comment for each.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 356, 'Move one thought from "what is wrong with me" to "what is happening right now," and answer the second question only.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 357, 'Read a message that bothered you three times, once as an insult, once as neutral, once as clumsy kindness. Note which reading has the most evidence.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 358, 'Redirect a thought about a mistake at work toward one thing you can do about it before you leave today.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 359, 'Shrink a thought to its smallest true version. "I ruined everything" might become "I sent the email late."'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 360, 'Practice noticing thoughts about the weather, the news or a stranger''s face today, and steering each one back to what you actually know.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 361, 'Answer a thought that says you cannot handle an autumn of changes with a list of what is staying the same.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 362, 'Pause before agreeing with a thought that calls something a failure, and ask what a partial success would look like.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 363, 'Convert one worried thought about a future bill, visit or deadline into a single calendar entry with a time to deal with it.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 364, 'Find the kindest true sentence you can say about a moment you keep replaying, and write it beneath the replay.'),
  ('redirecting-unhelpful-thoughts', 365, 'Write the fair version of a thought on a card and tuck it into your winter coat pocket to find on a cold morning.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 1, 'Pick a bedtime for tonight and set an alarm thirty minutes before it as your cue to start winding down.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 2, 'Put your phone somewhere out of reach from bed tonight and use a plain alarm clock if you need one.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 3, 'Dim the lights in the room you spend the evening in an hour before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 4, 'Write tomorrow''s to-do list before you get into bed so your mind can stop holding it.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 5, 'Do five minutes of gentle stretching before bed, slow and easy.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 6, 'Skip caffeine after noon today and notice how the evening feels.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 7, 'Take a warm shower or bath in the hour before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 8, 'Keep your bedroom a little cooler tonight, open a window or lower the heat.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 9, 'Read a few pages of a paper book or magazine in bed instead of a screen.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 10, 'Do a slow breath count in bed: in for four, out for six, for ten rounds.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 11, 'Get outside in daylight for ten minutes this morning. It helps your body know when night is.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 12, 'Finish eating at least two hours before bed tonight.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 13, 'If you are awake for more than twenty minutes in bed, get up, sit somewhere dim, and return when sleepy.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 14, 'Write down one worry that tends to visit at night and one thing you will do about it tomorrow.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 15, 'Make your bed this morning so it is ready for you tonight.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 16, 'Tidy the surfaces in your bedroom for five minutes so the room feels calmer.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 17, 'Try a body scan in bed: relax your feet, then your legs, and keep moving up until you reach your head.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 18, 'Listen to something quiet and slow, music, rain sounds, a calm audiobook, as you settle.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 19, 'Get up at the same time tomorrow as you did today, even if last night was rough.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 20, 'Keep the last hour of your evening free of work email and news.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 21, 'Do a two-minute gratitude review in bed: three good moments from the day.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 22, 'If your mind is busy, imagine a place you love in detail, the light, the sounds, the temperature.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 23, 'Swap your usual evening drink for a caffeine-free herbal tea or warm milk.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 24, 'Take a short walk after dinner tonight to give your body a gentle signal that the day is ending.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 25, 'Change into sleep clothes at the same time each evening this week, starting tonight.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 26, 'Write a single sentence in a notebook about how you slept last night. Patterns show up over time.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 27, 'Keep naps to twenty minutes and before mid-afternoon today, or skip them if you can.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 28, 'Say a short, kind sentence to yourself as you lie down, something like "The day is done. I can rest now."'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 29, 'Spend five minutes in the evening doing something with your hands, knitting, a puzzle, folding laundry.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 30, 'Look back at your sleep notes from this challenge and pick the one change that helped most. Keep it.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 31, 'Set a reminder on your calendar for tonight''s wind-down hour, and treat it like an appointment you would keep for a friend.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 32, 'Turn off overhead lights after dinner and use a single lamp instead.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 33, 'Close the curtains or blinds before it gets fully dark tonight so the room is ready when you are.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 34, 'Choose one calm activity for the last hour of the evening and do only that.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 35, 'Leave your laptop in another room once dinner is over.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 36, 'Brush your teeth an hour before bed tonight, so the signal that the day is over comes early.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 37, 'Put a glass of water on your nightstand before you settle so you will not need to get up for one.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 38, 'Sit by a window at dusk for a few minutes and let your eyes take in the fading light.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 39, 'Tonight, write down the time you turned the light off. Just the number, no comment.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 40, 'Warm your feet with socks or a hot water bottle as you get into bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 41, 'Put on a slow playlist while you do the dishes tonight and let the tempo set your pace for the evening.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 42, 'Swap the bright bathroom light for a nightlight or candle while you get ready for bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 43, 'Make tomorrow''s lunch tonight so the morning has one less job and the evening has a clear ending point.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 44, 'Lie on your back in bed and let your jaw go slack, then your shoulders, then your hands.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 45, 'Step outside for two minutes before bed and look up. The cool air and dark sky both help.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 46, 'Move your evening exercise earlier today so it finishes at least three hours before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 47, 'Charge your phone in the kitchen tonight instead of beside the bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 48, 'Ask someone you live with to keep the volume down after a certain time tonight, and agree on the time together.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 49, 'Let the last drink of the evening be water, and finish it an hour before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 50, 'Fold back the covers before you brush your teeth so getting into bed is the easiest thing in the house.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 51, 'Write three lines about the day in a notebook, then close it and leave it in another room.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 52, 'Sleep on your side with a pillow between your knees tonight and notice whether your hips and back settle more easily.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 53, 'Pick one thing you usually do late at night and move it to the afternoon today.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 54, 'Turn the clock face away from the bed so you cannot check the time in the night.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 55, 'Give your pillow a shake and a fluff, and flip it to the cool side before you lie down.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 56, 'Do ten slow shoulder rolls while you wait for the kettle to boil this evening.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 57, 'Keep pets off the bed tonight if they tend to wake you, and give them their own cozy spot nearby.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 58, 'Spend the last ten minutes before bed sitting in a chair, not lying down, so the bed stays just for sleep.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 59, 'Open the bedroom door or window for ten minutes before bed to freshen the air.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 60, 'Skip the late-night snack tonight and see whether you fall asleep more easily.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 61, 'Say goodnight out loud to the house, the day, or the people in it, and let that be the signal to stop.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 62, 'Choose a single word and repeat it silently each time you exhale in bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 63, 'Have dinner an hour earlier than usual tonight.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 64, 'Put a small notepad by the bed so any thought that arrives in the dark can be written down and released.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 65, 'Skip alcohol tonight and notice whether you wake less in the early hours.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 66, 'Rub a little unscented lotion into your hands and forearms as the last thing you do before turning off the light.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 67, 'Set your thermostat to drop a few degrees an hour before bed, or crack a window if the night is mild.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 68, 'Count backward from one hundred in bed, one number per breath.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 69, 'Wash your face with warm water and then splash it with cool water before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 70, 'Sort out tomorrow''s clothes tonight and lay them over a chair.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 71, 'Read something dull on purpose tonight, an instruction manual or a reference book, and let it lull you.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 72, 'Sit outside on a porch or step after dark for five minutes and listen to the evening sounds.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 73, 'Watch the sunset if you can see it today. The change in light is a cue your body understands.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 74, 'Switch your phone''s screen to grayscale for the evening, or better, put it away.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 75, 'Tuck a lavender sachet or a tissue with a drop of oil near your pillow tonight.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 76, 'Clear the path from the bathroom to the bed for five minutes so nothing catches your foot in the dark.'),
