  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 280, 'Go to bed within thirty minutes of the same time you did on the last three nights.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 281, 'Find a dark spot to see the stars tonight if you live somewhere that allows it, and let the night sky settle you.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 282, 'Turn your bed toward a wall or away from the door, if you can, and see whether the room feels more restful.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 283, 'Breathe slowly through the left nostril only for a minute, gently holding the right closed, before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 284, 'Put your work bag in the car or the hallway this evening so nothing from the office is in sight.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 285, 'Soak in a warm bath while one slow song plays, then dry off and go straight to bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 286, 'Count back from when you need to wake to find tonight''s bedtime, and add fifteen minutes for good measure.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 287, 'Sip warm water with a slice of lemon in the evening instead of tea, and see whether it sits more easily.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 288, 'Fold the laundry in a dim room before bed, slowly, and let the repetition quiet you.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 289, 'Look at your bed from the doorway this morning and ask what one small change would make it more inviting tonight.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 290, 'Walk in the rain for a few minutes tonight if it is warm enough, then a dry towel and a warm bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 291, 'Bring a plant into the bedroom, or move one in from another room, and let it green the corner you see from bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 292, 'Set a gentle wake-up sound rather than a harsh one for tomorrow, so the night ends as softly as it began.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 293, 'Trace slow circles on the back of your own hand with a fingertip in bed, and notice how the small touch settles you.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 294, 'Breathe in for four, hold for seven, out for eight, four times, once you are lying down tonight.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 295, 'Put the day''s mail, bills, and papers in a drawer before dinner and leave them there until tomorrow.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 296, 'Take your walk in the late-afternoon sun today instead of after dinner, so daylight comes earlier and rest comes later.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 297, 'Lay a soft blanket at the foot of the bed for the middle of the night, in case you wake chilly.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 298, 'Spend a quiet minute in the bathroom with the light off before you go to bed, and let your eyes adjust.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 299, 'Choose a word for how you want to feel as you fall asleep, calm, safe, done, and repeat it slowly.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 300, 'Eat your last meal while it is still light out tonight, whenever that falls in the season you are in.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 301, 'Walk slowly from the front door to the bedroom, touching each doorframe as a small "goodnight."'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 302, 'Sleep under a light sheet only tonight if the night is warm, and notice whether you wake less often.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 303, 'Stretch your hips on the floor, one knee across the body, before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 304, 'Move your evening snack earlier, or drop it, and notice whether your stomach lets you sleep more easily.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 305, 'Ask a friend to text you at nine tonight with a single word: "bed." Send them the same tomorrow.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 306, 'Pause at the bedroom door and leave one worry outside, the way you would leave shoes.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 307, 'Yawn on purpose, three times in a row, in bed, and see whether real ones follow.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 308, 'Give tonight a soundtrack of nothing at all: no television, no music, no talk after nine.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 309, 'Wear a loose sleep mask and earplugs together tonight if both light and noise trouble you.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 310, 'Push your alarm ten minutes later tomorrow and go to bed ten minutes earlier tonight, and keep the difference.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 311, 'Sit in the garden, on a balcony, or by an open window with a blanket at dusk this fall, and watch the light go.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 312, 'On a long summer evening, close the blinds before sunset so your body is not fooled by the late light.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 313, 'On a short winter evening, keep a bright lamp on until dinner and then dim everything after, so the drop in light is clear.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 314, 'In spring, open the bedroom window for a while after dinner and let the fresh evening air into the room before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 315, 'Give your bedroom a seasonal switch tonight: a lighter or heavier blanket, whichever the weather calls for.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 316, 'Stroll a quiet street after a holiday meal instead of collapsing on the couch, then begin your wind-down.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 317, 'On the night before a big day, set out everything you need and then read something unrelated until sleepy.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 318, 'On the night after a hard day, give yourself an extra fifteen minutes of wind-down, not less.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 319, 'End the evening''s last conversation with "let''s talk tomorrow," and mean it.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 320, 'Notice whether a late dinner out tends to cost you sleep, and choose an earlier reservation next time.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 321, 'Stretch your neck and shoulders at your desk at the end of the workday, so tension does not travel home.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 322, 'Put a small dish of water on the radiator or run a humidifier tonight if the winter air is dry.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 323, 'Run a dehumidifier or open a window on a muggy night so the room does not feel close.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 324, 'Wear a lighter sleep shirt tonight and keep a sweater by the bed for the early hours.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 325, 'Flip your pillow to the cool side halfway through your wind-down, or use a cooling pillowcase.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 326, 'Take a hot bath on a cold night and get straight into a bed you warmed ahead of time.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 327, 'Sit outside for five minutes after dark on a clear autumn night, then go straight to bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 328, 'Stretch your wrists and fingers before bed if you type all day.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 329, 'On a night you have to work late, use a warm lamp, not the overhead light, and still stop thirty minutes before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 330, 'On a day off, resist the urge to sleep in past your usual time by more than an hour.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 331, 'On a travel night, bring one familiar thing from your bedtime routine, a pillowcase, a tea bag, a book.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 332, 'When guests are staying, agree on a quiet time for the house and honor it yourself.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 333, 'When the house is empty, keep your bedtime anyway, even if no one is watching.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 334, 'Warm a folded washcloth in the microwave and lay it over your eyes for a minute before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 335, 'Rest your feet on a heating pad for ten minutes before bed on a cold night.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 336, 'On a hot night, freeze a water bottle wrapped in a towel and tuck it at the foot of the bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 337, 'Skip dessert and sweet drinks after dinner tonight, and see whether you sleep more evenly.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 338, 'Ask a partner or housemate to take over one evening chore tonight so your wind-down starts sooner.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 339, 'Set the table for breakfast before bed so the morning is quieter and the evening ends with a small act of care.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 340, 'Write one sentence to your future self for tomorrow morning and leave it beside the kettle.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 341, 'Watch a short, gentle nature program in the early evening, then turn the screen off well before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 342, 'Play a quiet card game or work a puzzle with someone you live with as the evening''s last activity.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 343, 'On a rainy night, leave the window cracked and let the sound do the work.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 344, 'Rock gently in a chair or on the edge of the bed for a few minutes before you lie down.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 345, 'Program any smart bulbs you have to switch to warm and dim at the same hour every night.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 346, 'Pour a cup of decaf coffee in the evening if you miss the ritual more than the caffeine.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 347, 'Take the batteries out of a ticking clock in the bedroom, or move it to the hallway.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 348, 'Point your toes in bed, then flex them, then let your legs go heavy.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 349, 'Set a "last light" time for the whole house tonight and turn everything off together.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 350, 'Thank your body for the day''s work as you lie down, feet, hands, back, eyes.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 351, 'Take a warm, slow shower after an evening workout so your body cools gradually before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 352, 'Set a soft chime on your phone for wind-down time, then leave the phone in the kitchen.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 353, 'Sip a small cup of warm broth in the evening instead of a heavy snack.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 354, 'Smooth and tuck the bed before you get in, even if you did not make it this morning.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 355, 'Open the window, turn off the lights, and look at the stars from bed for a few minutes.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 356, 'Roll a tennis ball under each foot for a minute before bed.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 357, 'Rest a hand on your chest in bed and listen for your own heartbeat for a minute.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 358, 'Put a sleep timer on your bedroom fan or heater so it turns off after you drop off.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 359, 'Keep a small towel by the bed on hot nights to wipe your face and neck without getting up.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 360, 'Sit on the floor with your back against the bed for a few minutes before you climb in.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 361, 'Slide a pillow under your knees tonight if your lower back tends to ache.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 362, 'Leave the last chapter of your book unread so you have something to look forward to tomorrow night.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 363, 'Keep a Friday night the same as a weeknight: same bedtime, same dim lights, no late night just because it is the weekend.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 364, 'Give Sunday evening a reset: sheets changed, alarm checked, clothes out, lights low.'),
  ('winding-down-for-better-sleep', 365, 'Look back at everything you have tried this year, and choose the three evening habits you will keep for good.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 1, 'Write down the exact words your inner critic used today. Notice its tone.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 2, 'Put your hand on your heart for thirty seconds and say silently, "This is hard right now."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 3, 'Think of something you did imperfectly today and say, "That is what learning looks like."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 4, 'Write one sentence to yourself that you would write to a friend who made the same mistake.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 5, 'Notice when you call yourself a name today and replace it with your actual first name.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 6, 'List three things you did today that were good enough. Not perfect. Good enough.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 7, 'When the critic speaks, ask it: "Whose voice is this really?" Sometimes it is someone from long ago.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 8, 'Give yourself permission to do one thing at eighty percent today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 9, 'Write down one thing you like about how you treat other people.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 10, 'Say "thank you" when someone compliments you today, with nothing added.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 11, 'Catch a "should have" and rewrite it as "next time I could."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 12, 'Take a photo of yourself and find one thing to say kindly about the person in it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 13, 'Notice one small kindness you showed yourself today, a break, a meal, a rest, and name it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 14, 'Write a short note from your future self, ten years on, to the you of today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 15, 'Remember a time you were hard on yourself and it did not help. Give the critic the day off.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 16, 'Do one thing today purely because you enjoy it, with no productivity attached.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 17, 'When you make a mistake today, say out loud, "Everyone does this sometimes."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 18, 'Write down a strength you have that you rarely give yourself credit for.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 19, 'Notice a moment of self-criticism and place both feet on the floor and breathe out slowly before responding.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 20, 'Ask someone you trust to tell you one thing they appreciate about you, and let it in.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 21, 'Forgive yourself for one specific thing tonight, in writing.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 22, 'Treat your body with one gesture of care today, a stretch, a slower meal, an earlier night.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 23, 'Write down the critic''s harshest line and then answer it in the voice of someone who loves you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 24, 'Say no to one thing today that you would only be doing to prove yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 25, 'Spend two minutes listing what you have handled in the past year. Read it twice.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 26, 'Notice the difference today between "I did something wrong" and "I am wrong." Only the first is ever true.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 27, 'Choose a small reward for finishing something today and actually take it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 28, 'Write "I am doing my best with what I have today" and put it where you will see it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 29, 'When you compare yourself to someone today, name one thing you are not seeing about their life.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 30, 'Read back over your notes from this challenge and write one line about how the critic''s voice has changed.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 31, 'Count how many times the critic speaks before lunch today. Just tally, no arguing back yet.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 32, 'Give your inner critic a name that makes it a little less scary, then greet it by that name the next time it shows up.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 33, 'Pick one task you have been avoiding because you might do it badly, and spend ten minutes on it anyway.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 34, 'Say "I am allowed to be a beginner at this" out loud before trying something new today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 35, 'Write the critic''s favorite sentence on a slip of paper, then write a fairer version underneath and keep only the second one.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 36, 'Notice today when the critic uses the word "always" or "never," and quietly correct it to "sometimes."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 37, 'Look in the mirror while brushing your teeth and say one neutral, honest thing about yourself, nothing harsh and nothing forced.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 38, 'Before a meeting or appointment today, tell yourself what you hope to bring rather than what you are afraid of getting wrong.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 39, 'When you finish something today, pause for a full breath before moving on, and let the finishing count.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 40, 'Think of a mistake from years ago that still stings, and write down what it taught you that you still use.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 41, 'Ask yourself at dinner: "What would I say to a coworker who had the day I just had?" Then say it to yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 42, 'Replace one "I have to" with "I get to" today and notice whether the critic gets quieter.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 43, 'Write down three ordinary things you did well this week that nobody noticed, including you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 44, 'Take a walk outside and, each time a self-critical thought arrives, name one thing you can see instead.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 45, 'Set a timer for five minutes and write to yourself in the second person, "You are someone who...", finishing the sentence as many ways as you can.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 46, 'Notice when you apologize today for something that needed no apology, and let the next one go unsaid.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 47, 'Choose one thing you are self-conscious about and wear it, do it, or show it today without explaining it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 48, 'Write down what the critic says you should be doing with your evenings, then decide for yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 49, 'Tell someone about a mistake you made this week, plainly, without self-deprecating jokes.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 50, 'When you catch yourself rehearsing an old embarrassment, say, "That was then," and describe where you are right now.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 51, 'Say the critic''s harshest line in a cartoon voice and notice how much less authority it has.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 52, 'Spend a few minutes tonight listing what went right today before you list what went wrong.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 53, 'Notice a moment today when you did something well, and let yourself say "I did that" without adding a "but."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 54, 'Write a two-line reference letter for yourself as if you were a manager who liked working with you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 55, 'Pay attention to your posture after a self-critical thought today, and gently lift your chin an inch.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 56, 'When the critic points out a flaw today, ask it: "And what is the kind thing to do about that?"'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 57, 'Cook or order a meal you actually want tonight, without earning it first.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 58, 'Write down one rule you hold yourself to that you would never impose on anyone else.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 59, 'Give yourself the same amount of time to get ready this morning that you would give a guest, no rushing yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 60, 'Recall a compliment you brushed off in the past month and write it down as if it were true.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 61, 'Do one household task imperfectly and on purpose today, then leave it and walk away.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 62, 'Listen for the critic''s tone of voice today, sharp, sighing, sarcastic, and describe it in a single word.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 63, 'Practice saying "I don''t know yet" today instead of "I should know this."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 64, 'Notice whether the critic is louder when you are hungry or tired, and meet the need before you answer the thought.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 65, 'Write a note to the part of you that keeps trying, and thank it for showing up again today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 66, 'When you compare your work to someone else''s today, name one thing yours does that theirs does not.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 67, 'Pick a photo of yourself as a child and say to that child the words you needed to hear back then.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 68, 'Ask a friend what they think you are too hard on yourself about, and just listen.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 69, 'Set your phone wallpaper or a sticky note to one sentence you would say to a struggling friend.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 70, 'Try describing a mistake you made today using only facts, no adjectives, and see how much shorter it gets.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 71, 'Skip the mental replay tonight: when you climb into bed, tell yourself the day is finished and you did enough.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 72, 'Before you send an email or message today, resist rereading it more than twice.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 73, 'Notice when the critic speaks in your parent''s or teacher''s words today, and answer in your own.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 74, 'Start one sentence today with "I am proud that I" and finish it honestly.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 75, 'Write down what you would lose if you stopped criticizing yourself, then check whether any of it is real.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 76, 'Sit somewhere sunny for five minutes and let yourself be a person on a break, not a project.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 77, 'When you drop something or bump into something today, say "oops" and nothing more.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 78, 'Make a short list of what you were good at as a teenager and notice which of those things are still in you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 79, 'Say to yourself, "I can be disappointed without being disgusted," the next time something goes wrong today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 80, 'Pick a strength a friend has told you about and look for one moment you use it today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 81, 'Send yourself a message tonight that starts with "Hey, I saw how you handled..." and finish it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 82, 'Give your hands a moment of care today, lotion, warm water, a stretch, and notice it as a small act of respect.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 83, 'Reread a piece of your own writing, a message, a note, a post, and find one line you like.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 84, 'Try finishing a task to "done" rather than "perfect" today and leave the polishing for another time.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 85, 'Notice a body-focused criticism today and reply with one thing that part of your body did for you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 86, 'Ask yourself before bed: "Was I fair to myself today?" and answer in one sentence.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 87, 'Turn a harsh "Why did you do that?" into a curious "What was going on for me then?"'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 88, 'Draw a quick doodle of what your inner critic looks like, then give it a smaller chair.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 89, 'When you finish a workday, name the thing you did best, not the thing you left undone.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 90, 'Remember someone who was patient with you when you were learning, and borrow their patience for yourself today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 91, 'Put on clothes that feel comfortable today without commenting on how you look in them.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 92, 'Write down one thing the critic protects you from, and decide whether you still need that protection.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 93, 'Praise yourself out loud in the car or the shower for one thing, even if it feels silly.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 94, 'Notice today when you say "just" about your own work, "I just did a little," and drop the word.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 95, 'Tell yourself the truth about a skill you have grown in this year, and say it without downplaying it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 96, 'Ask what you would need to hear right now, then say it to yourself in a warm voice.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 97, 'Let one typo, one wrinkle, or one crumb go unfixed today and see that nothing collapses.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 98, 'Write a short "permission slip" for the day: "Today I am allowed to..." and sign it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 99, 'When you catch a sigh of frustration at yourself, follow it with a slower, kinder breath out.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 100, 'Practice receiving help today, and let "thank you" be the whole response.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 101, 'Name the feeling under the criticism the next time it shows up today: fear, shame, tiredness, or something else.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 102, 'Notice the first self-critical thought of the morning and answer it before you get out of bed.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 103, 'On your commute or morning walk, think of one thing you handled well yesterday and let it set the tone.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 104, 'Write the words "good enough" on your to-do list next to one task, and mean it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 105, 'Tell a coworker or friend about something you are learning, using the word "learning" instead of "struggling."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 106, 'When you make a small error at work today, fix it and move on without a speech to yourself about it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 107, 'Take your lunch break fully today, away from your desk, as a person who deserves a break.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 108, 'Catch the critic predicting failure this afternoon and reply, "We will see," and nothing else.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 109, 'At the end of the workday, write one line about what you contributed, however ordinary.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 110, 'Look at a project you finished a while ago and notice one thing you would not have been able to do earlier.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 111, 'Ask yourself what standard you are measuring yourself against today, and whether you ever agreed to it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 112, 'Say "that is a reasonable thing to feel" to yourself the next time an emotion arrives that you would rather not have.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 113, 'Spend five minutes writing about a talent you have that you consider unimportant, and take it seriously for once.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 114, 'Remember a time you were kind to a stranger, and let that be evidence about who you are.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 115, 'Leave your bed unmade or the dishes for an hour and notice if the critic tries to make it mean something about you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 116, 'Put your hand on your shoulder for a moment, as a friend would, when you feel the critic''s tone rising.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 117, 'Say aloud today: "I made a choice with the information I had," about a decision you have been second-guessing.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 118, 'Write down two things you have improved at without anyone teaching you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 119, 'Try answering the critic in the third person: "She is tired, not lazy," or "He is learning, not failing."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 120, 'Notice when you minimize a success today with "it was nothing," and correct it to "I worked at that."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 121, 'Ask the critic what it is afraid will happen if you go easy on yourself, and write down the answer.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 122, 'Give yourself an early night tonight without calling it lazy.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 123, 'Spend a minute looking at your own hands and thinking of what they have made, carried, or fixed.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 124, 'Compliment yourself on something you do every day that requires skill, driving, cooking, listening, typing.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 125, 'Notice a moment today where you did the right thing when no one was watching, and let yourself count it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 126, 'Rewrite "I am bad at this" as "I have not practiced this much" and see how it changes what you do next.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 127, 'Take a break in the middle of a hard task today instead of pushing through in punishment mode.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 128, 'Say a kind word to yourself in the language or accent of someone who has loved you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 129, 'Write a one-line apology to yourself for something harsh you said in your head this week.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 130, 'Listen to a song you loved at sixteen and think about what that version of you would admire in you now.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 131, 'Find one thing in your home you made or chose well, and admire it for a moment.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 132, 'When a mistake surfaces today, ask "What would make this better?" instead of "What is wrong with me?"'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 133, 'Pick a quality you admire in a friend and look for a small sign of it in yourself before the day ends.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 134, 'Rate your day on kindness to yourself rather than on productivity tonight, and see how the number differs.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 135, 'Try eating one meal today without a screen and without commenting on the food or your choices.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 136, 'Wear something you like today because you like it, and let that be the whole reason.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 137, 'Notice if you are rehearsing a conversation for the tenth time, and let yourself stop at nine.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 138, 'Write a list titled "Things I did not fail at today" and fill in five lines.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 139, 'Tell yourself "you are allowed to change your mind" when the critic calls a new decision flaky.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 140, 'Spend a few minutes outdoors and let the trees, rain, or sky be indifferent to your flaws in a comforting way.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 141, 'Find a small object, a stone, a coin, a button, to keep in your pocket as a reminder to speak gently to yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 142, 'Catch one "everyone else can do this" and check whether "everyone" is really more than two people.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 143, 'Give yourself credit for asking a question today instead of pretending to know.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 144, 'Before bed, tell yourself one thing you are looking forward to, as a gift rather than a demand.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 145, 'Notice how you speak to yourself when you are running late, and try one softer sentence on the way.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 146, 'Take a slow drink of water and use the pause to let a harsh thought pass without answering it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 147, 'Write down what you would tell a younger sibling who was ashamed of the same thing you are ashamed of.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 148, 'Say "I am allowed to take up space" before you walk into a room today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 149, 'Practice describing yourself to a stranger in three sentences with no negative words.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 150, 'Look at your calendar for tomorrow and remove one thing you added only to prove you are not lazy.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 151, 'When the critic speaks today, picture it as a nervous friend rather than an enemy, and answer it accordingly.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 152, 'Sort a memory of a mistake into two piles: what was in your control and what was not. Keep only the first.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 153, 'Do a quick body scan for tension after the next self-critical thought, and loosen whatever tightened.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 154, 'Let yourself rest for ten minutes in the afternoon without an explanation.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 155, 'Write a thank-you note to yourself for a hard season you got through.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 156, 'Say "I noticed that" instead of "I should have noticed sooner" the next time you spot a problem today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 157, 'Do something a little clumsily today on purpose, a new recipe, a new route, and let it be fine.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 158, 'Pick a phrase your critic uses that sounds wise but is really just cruel, and retire it for the day.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 159, 'Look for one moment today when you were patient with someone, and give yourself the same patience tonight.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 160, 'Ask a family member what they remember about you doing well as a kid, and write it down.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 161, 'Notice a compliment you give someone else today, and check whether you would ever say it to yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 162, 'When the day gets away from you, say, "I will start again from here," and start from there.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 163, 'Sit with a cup of something warm and spend a minute listing what you have kept going this year.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 164, 'Reply to a harsh inner comment with, "Noted, and I am still going to be kind to myself."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 165, 'Set aside one item on your list that you were only doing out of guilt, and let it wait.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 166, 'Write the sentence "I am not behind, I am here," and read it back when the critic compares your timeline to others.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 167, 'Tell yourself the story of a time you recovered from a setback, all the way through to the recovery.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 168, 'Give yourself full credit for a job done at seventy percent of what you had planned.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 169, 'Try a small experiment today: answer the critic with a joke and see if it loosens its grip.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 170, 'Watch for perfectionism in one specific task today and stop when the task works, not when it gleams.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 171, 'Say goodnight to yourself tonight with the same warmth you would use with a child.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 172, 'Take a walk in the cold and notice that the critic gets quieter when your senses are busy.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 173, 'On a rainy day, stay in and reread a note or card someone once wrote about you, and believe it for the length of the reading.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 174, 'Notice the critic''s response when you rest on a weekend, and remind it that rest is part of the work.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 175, 'Plant something, water something, or tend to a houseplant, and let yourself be gentle with a living thing, including you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 176, 'Write a note to yourself for the next time you feel like a failure, seal it, and keep it in a drawer.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 177, 'Think about what you would like a friend to remember about you, and let that be the truer measure than today''s slip.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 178, 'In the first warm evening of the season, sit outside and list three things you have done this year that took courage.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 179, 'Notice the critic''s reaction when you are around people who are doing well, and offer yourself an honest encouragement.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 180, 'Ask yourself, "Is this a fact or a feeling?" when the critic makes a claim today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 181, 'Set down a task the moment the critic starts narrating it, breathe, and pick it up again in your own voice.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 182, 'Spend a minute noticing how a pet, a plant, or a child accepts you without evaluation.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 183, 'Give a younger colleague or a newcomer some grace today, and note how easy it was compared with giving it to yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 184, 'Write "I did the best I could with what I knew then" about one specific past decision.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 185, 'When you sit down to a meal, silently thank yourself for making sure you were fed.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 186, 'Rehearse a kinder response to a mistake you tend to make often, so it is ready when you need it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 187, 'Find a picture of a place you love and imagine your inner critic having to be quiet there.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 188, 'Think of a time you were wrong and admitted it. Give yourself credit for the admitting.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 189, 'Notice how many "should" sentences you say to yourself before noon and cut the count in half by evening.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 190, 'Hold a warm mug in both hands and tell yourself, "I am on my own side today."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 191, 'When you feel unprepared for something today, say, "I will figure it out as I go," and give yourself that trust.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 192, 'Ask someone who knows you well to name a mistake they remember you making. Notice how small it seems to them.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 193, 'Leave a task at a natural stopping point today and resist the urge to call yourself a quitter.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 194, 'Write down a harsh belief about yourself and then list two pieces of evidence that contradict it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 195, 'Tell yourself before a difficult conversation: "I do not have to be perfect, only present."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 196, 'Practice saying "I am learning" three times today in place of "I am terrible at this."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 197, 'Take the stairs, the bus, or the long way today and use the time to think of one thing you like about who you are becoming.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 198, 'Set a boundary with the critic: it may speak, but only in complete, honest sentences.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 199, 'Turn off the lights a little earlier tonight and say "enough for today" as you do.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 200, 'Write a one-sentence forecast of how you will feel about today''s mistake in a month.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 201, 'Find one person to tell "I am proud of myself for" something small, and say it without laughing it off.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 202, 'Pause after a self-critical thought and ask, "Would I let someone else say this to me?"'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 203, 'Look at your reflection in a shop window today and offer a nod instead of a critique.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 204, 'Choose a slower pace for one chore this evening and do it with care instead of speed.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 205, 'Write a list of people who have been kind to you, and consider that they saw something worth being kind to.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 206, 'When the critic says you are wasting time, ask what you are actually doing and whether it is restful.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 207, 'Spend two minutes listing skills you learned in the past five years that you now take for granted.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 208, 'Practice saying "I made a mistake" without adding "as usual."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 209, 'Hum or sing while you do a task today and notice how hard it is to criticize yourself while humming.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 210, 'Consider what your inner critic would say if it were on your side, and write down its new script.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 211, 'Give yourself credit at the end of the day for every task you started, not just the ones you finished.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 212, 'Sit in a park or a coffee shop and notice that no one there is grading you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 213, 'Say something kind to yourself in a whisper before you answer the phone or open your email today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 214, 'Take a short nap or a lie-down this weekend and let it be a gift rather than a lapse.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 215, 'Look at something you have kept alive, a plant, a friendship, a habit, and give yourself credit for the tending.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 216, 'Write "still here, still trying" on a card and tuck it into your wallet or bag.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 217, 'Practice noticing self-judgment during exercise or a walk today and shifting to what your body can do.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 218, 'Reframe a "failed" attempt from this year as a first draft and name what the second draft could keep.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 219, 'Ask yourself what you would let a beloved coworker off the hook for, and let yourself off for the same thing.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 220, 'Read the last message you sent to someone who was upset, and notice how gentle you were. Use those words on yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 221, 'Try cooking one dish without checking a recipe, and let the outcome be an experiment rather than a verdict.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 222, 'Notice today whether the critic shows up mostly in the morning, the evening, or at work, and plan one kind sentence for that time.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 223, 'When you feel behind on a chore, say, "It will get done when it gets done," and let your shoulders drop.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 224, 'Write a description of yourself from the point of view of a neighbor who sees you come and go.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 225, 'Say "I am enough for today" while you lock your door in the morning.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 226, 'Give your future self a kind sentence in your calendar for next week, and let it surprise you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 227, 'Recall a moment you helped someone this year and let it outweigh one moment you were unhelpful.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 228, 'Do something imperfect in front of other people today, and notice that the world went on.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 229, 'Before a decision today, listen for the critic''s "you always get this wrong" and answer with one time you got it right.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 230, 'Do something with your hands this evening, drawing, folding, kneading, and let it be about the doing, not the result.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 231, 'Write down a small victory from the summer or the winter that you never told anyone about.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 232, 'Spend five minutes in the sun or by a window and let yourself be warmed without earning it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 233, 'Keep a list today of every time you catch the critic, and give yourself a point for each catch rather than a mark against you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 234, 'Say "I am not my worst moment" when the critic replays one of them tonight.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 235, 'Notice today whether you criticize yourself for being tired, and give yourself the rest instead of the lecture.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 236, 'Try telling a friend one thing you like about yourself, and let them agree without arguing.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 237, 'Look at a to-do list from last month and notice how much of it you handled without remembering the effort.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 238, 'Ask a coworker for feedback today and listen for the good parts as carefully as the corrections.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 239, 'When you spill, trip, or forget today, say, "Being human, as planned."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 240, 'Write a kind message to a version of yourself from a hard time, and read it as if it were addressed to you now.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 241, 'Take a picture of something you accomplished today, however small, and keep it as evidence.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 242, 'Notice a "should" that keeps you from asking for help, then ask anyway.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 243, 'Spend a moment before work naming one thing about your work you are genuinely good at.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 244, 'When you finish a phone call or meeting today, say something kind about how you showed up in it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 245, 'Take a detour to somewhere pretty today and let the view speak louder than the critic.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 246, 'Write down a criticism you fear from others and then check whether anyone has actually said it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 247, 'Ask yourself tonight: "What did I need today, and did I give it to myself?"'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 248, 'Let a friend pay for coffee or do a favor today, and practice accepting without insisting you owe them.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 249, 'Notice the critic in a group setting today and answer with a quiet "I belong here as much as anyone."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 250, 'Change one word in your self-talk today: "failed" to "tried," "lazy" to "tired," "stupid" to "new."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 251, 'Take three slow breaths before you check your work today, and go in as an editor, not a judge.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 252, 'Try speaking to yourself as a coach who wants you to win rather than a referee waiting for a foul.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 253, 'Make a list of five things about your character that you would not trade for someone else''s talents.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 254, 'When you miss a workout, a deadline, or a call today, tell yourself what you would tell a friend who did the same.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 255, 'Ask what your best friend would say about the mistake that is on your mind, and write their answer.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 256, 'Sit quietly for a minute and see if you can hear the critic without believing it, like a radio in another room.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 257, 'Send yourself a voice note saying one kind thing, and listen to it back.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 258, 'Take stock of one thing you did this week purely out of care for someone, and let it count toward who you are.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 259, 'Notice when the critic uses "everyone thinks" today, and ask it to name one actual person.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 260, 'Cook breakfast for yourself the way you would for a guest, or at least sit down to eat it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 261, 'Give yourself three attempts at a task today, and treat the first two as practice rather than proof.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 262, 'When someone corrects you today, say, "Thanks, good to know," and skip the inner replay.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 263, 'Tell yourself that a bad hour does not make a bad day, then move to the next hour.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 264, 'Set a small goal this morning and celebrate meeting it this evening with a real pause, not a shrug.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 265, 'Practice "and" instead of "but" today: "I was late, and I still did good work."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 266, 'Write down what you are afraid people would think if you stopped being so hard on yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 267, 'Rest your eyes for a minute and picture the critic shrinking to the size of a mouse.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 268, 'Look for a moment today when you handled something calmly, and tell yourself that you are the sort of person who does that.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 269, 'Pick one habit you shame yourself for and describe it in neutral words, as a scientist would.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 270, 'Give yourself permission to say "I am not sure" in a conversation today without following it with an excuse.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 271, 'Notice the critic when you cannot remember something today, and reply, "My mind is full, not failing."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 272, 'Write down one thing you are getting better at, even if the progress is slow.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 273, 'Pay for something small for yourself today, a flower, a pastry, a book, without justifying it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 274, 'Practice pausing for one full breath between a mistake and your first thought about it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 275, 'Sit with a disappointment today without turning it into a verdict on your whole life.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 276, 'Say to the critic, "You can come back later," and give yourself an hour of peace.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 277, 'Ask someone you love to tell you about a time you got something right, and let it be true.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 278, 'Reflect on a decision you made under pressure this year and give yourself credit for deciding at all.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 279, 'Try a task you are not good at, badly, for five minutes, and notice that you survived.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 280, 'Notice the difference between "I am lazy" and "I am not motivated right now," and use the second one.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 281, 'Buy or borrow a book you loved as a child and let yourself enjoy it without calling it silly.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 282, 'Let someone see your unfinished work today and notice that they did not react the way the critic predicted.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 283, 'Walk through your home and notice the things that show you take care of yourself, then say so.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 284, 'Answer the critic''s "you are not good enough" with "good enough for what?" and wait for a real answer.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 285, 'Give yourself the last word tonight: after the critic''s summary of the day, add one kind, true sentence.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 286, 'Do one thing today that a past version of you would have found hard, and notice that it is now easy.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 287, 'Spend a few minutes looking at old photos and speaking kindly about the person in each one.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 288, 'Say "that is a fair point, and I will handle it" when the critic has an actual point today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 289, 'Notice when you skip a compliment you deserve because you are waiting for a bigger achievement to count.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 290, 'Sort today''s mistakes into "matters in a year" and "does not," and let the second pile go.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 291, 'Turn one of your inner "why can''t you" questions into a "how could I," and answer it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 292, 'Think about how you talk to yourself when you drive, and make one change on your next trip.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 293, 'Write down something a mentor or teacher once praised you for, and look for it in your work today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 294, 'Take a photo of the sky and think of the critic as one cloud, passing through.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 295, 'Let a mistake at work stay a mistake at work today, without following you home.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 296, 'Give yourself a full ten minutes of doing nothing and say "this is allowed" if the critic protests.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 297, 'Write a list of three things you are not going to feel bad about anymore, and read it aloud.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 298, 'Practice telling a story about yourself with the mistakes left in and the shame left out.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 299, 'When you feel ashamed today, put a hand on your cheek for a moment, the way you would comfort a friend.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 300, 'Check if evenings are when the critic gets loudest, and plan a kind routine for that hour.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 301, 'Ask yourself who taught you to expect perfection, and decide whether they still get a vote.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 302, 'Write a short list of what you did right in a relationship that ended, and stop the list at the good parts.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 303, 'Give yourself a small, quiet cheer when you finish a chore today, like a friend on the sidelines would.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 304, 'Try a new small thing today, a recipe, a route, a word, without treating the first attempt as the final grade.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 305, 'Name one thing you are looking forward to becoming, and speak to yourself as someone already on the way.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 306, 'Notice a body sensation that comes with the critic''s voice, a tight jaw or a knot in your stomach, and soften that spot.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 307, 'Look at a bill you paid, a form you filed, or an errand you ran this week and count it as competence.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 308, 'Say "I forgive myself for not knowing then what I know now" about one specific regret.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 309, 'Sit with a friend, in person or on the phone, and tell them one thing you are proud of without a disclaimer.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 310, 'Notice today when you use "lazy" about yourself and replace it with a description of what you actually needed.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 311, 'Write a kind caption for the day, as if it were a photo in an album a loving friend keeps of you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 312, 'Open a window or step onto a porch this morning and say one hopeful sentence about the day to yourself.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 313, 'Reply to the critic''s "you are so behind" with a list of three things you are actually on top of.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 314, 'Make a cup of tea or coffee slowly today and drink it as someone who deserves a nice moment.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 315, 'Look for the critic in how you handle a compliment at work today, and let the compliment land without deflecting.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 316, 'Let yourself leave a party, a call, or a gathering early tonight without a story about being a bad guest.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 317, 'Ask a trusted person what they would say if they could hear how you talk to yourself, and take it in.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 318, 'Practice describing one of your quirks with fondness instead of embarrassment today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 319, 'Keep a pen handy and write "kind" in the margin every time you catch a harsh thought at your desk today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 320, 'Spend a minute in the shower tonight thanking yourself for one hard thing you did today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 321, 'Set a gentle alarm label for tomorrow morning, like "You''ve got this," and let it be the first words you read.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 322, 'Try walking a little slower on your way somewhere today and notice how the critic hurries you.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 323, 'Pick one old grudge you hold against yourself and decide whether it has served its sentence.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 324, 'Look at a piece of work you were nervous to share, and find one thing in it that was brave.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 325, 'Give yourself a small break from mirrors today and see if the critic has less to say.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 326, 'Tell yourself "I showed up" after a hard conversation today, and let that be the headline.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 327, 'Think of a mistake you made that later turned into something good, and tell yourself that story tonight.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 328, 'Practice the phrase "that is one way to see it" when the critic offers its verdict today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 329, 'Watch how you talk to yourself while getting dressed, and swap one unkind word for a neutral one.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 330, 'Ask yourself what the critic would need to hear to settle down, and then say it.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 331, 'Take a break to stretch this afternoon and thank your body for carrying you through the morning.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 332, 'Notice today when you are performing competence for others, and let yourself be ordinary for an hour.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 333, 'Write down what you have already survived that you once thought you could not.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 334, 'Do a small favor for your tomorrow self tonight, laying out clothes, prepping breakfast, and tell yourself why.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 335, 'Notice when the critic calls a rest day "wasted," and rename it "recovered."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 336, 'Reflect on a friendship that has lasted, and let it prove you are someone worth staying with.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 337, 'Ask yourself what you would say to a teammate who missed a shot, then say it about your own miss today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 338, 'Spend a moment before sleep noticing a place in your life where you have done better than you expected.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 339, 'Stand outside on a cold morning and say, "I am tougher than the critic says," before going back in.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 340, 'Try greeting a challenge today with "let''s see what happens" instead of "I will probably mess this up."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 341, 'Give yourself a pass on one comparison today: when a friend''s news arrives, just be glad for them.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 342, 'Write a single kind sentence about yourself on a fogged mirror or a steamy window.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 343, 'Notice when the critic questions a purchase, a meal, or a choice, and answer with "I am allowed to choose."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 344, 'Practice responding to praise from a coworker with a simple "I appreciate that" today.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 345, 'Tell your reflection at the end of the day, "We got through it," and mean the "we."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 346, 'Choose a task you usually rush to get it over with, and do it with unhurried care instead.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 347, 'Spend five minutes remembering the small skills you had to learn for your job and give yourself credit for each.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 348, 'Write the phrase "mistakes are information" on a sticky note and put it on your monitor or fridge.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 349, 'Notice one moment today when you were competent without noticing, and notice it now.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 350, 'Try apologizing to yourself for a harsh thought, out loud, and then move on with the day.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 351, 'Ask yourself who benefits when you are hard on yourself, and whether the answer is anyone at all.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 352, 'Give yourself an honest performance review tonight that includes the phrase "meets expectations."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 353, 'Practice taking a compliment about your appearance today with a plain "thank you."'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 354, 'Write a note to the version of you who will make a mistake next week, letting them know they are still welcome.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 355, 'Look at a photo from a hard year and tell the person in it that they made it through.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 356, 'Hold an ice cube or run cold water over your wrists during a spiral of self-criticism, and start again once it passes.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 357, 'Let a weekend morning be slow, and if the critic calls it lazy, call it rest.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 358, 'Say "I did not know that yet" the next time you learn something you think you should have known.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 359, 'Make your bed or clear a surface today and let the neatness be a gift to yourself, not a test.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 360, 'Notice when you are speaking to yourself in the voice of a critic from a job you left long ago, and let them go too.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 361, 'Spend a minute thinking about someone who would be proud of you today, and imagine what they would say.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 362, 'Write down a sentence you would like the critic to say more often, and read it to yourself when it shows up.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 363, 'Practice "so what?" today: when the critic points out a flaw, ask what would actually happen next.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 364, 'Take a different route home and give the critic no familiar cue to start its speech.'),
  ('softening-the-inner-critic', 365, 'Recognize one moment today where you were generous with yourself, and let it be a pattern rather than a fluke.'),
