  ('reaching-out-to-people', 272, 'Chat with a parent at the school pickup line instead of waiting in the car.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 273, 'Send a friend a question about their kids, their work, or their team, whatever they talk about most.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 274, 'Ask a coworker how they got into the work they do.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 275, 'Message a friend during a game, a show, or an awards night and react to it together in real time.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 276, 'Ask an acquaintance to become a friend by suggesting a second hangout after the first.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 277, 'Bring a neighbor a bag of extra produce, baked goods, or leftovers and stay to chat.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 278, 'Ask a friend what they wish people asked them about more often.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 279, 'Tell a coworker or classmate about a place you love and offer to take them there.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 280, 'Check that a friend got home okay the morning after a long night out.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 281, 'Ask a family member what song, movie, or meal reminds them of you.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 282, 'Attend a religious service, a meditation group, or a community circle and stay for the coffee afterward.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 283, 'Ask a friend if you can call them on your commute home today.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 284, 'Tell someone the honest reason you have been out of touch, and that you are glad to be back.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 285, 'Ask a coworker about a hobby you have heard them mention in passing.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 286, 'Meet a friend at a playground, a dog park, or a track so kids or pets can play while you talk.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 287, 'Send a message to your group chat suggesting a real date for the thing you keep saying you will do.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 288, 'Ask a neighbor what they are planting, building, or fixing this weekend.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 289, 'Reply to a newsletter, a podcast, or a creator you follow with a short, sincere note.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 290, 'Describe your week in three words to a friend and ask for theirs.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 291, 'Take a snack or coffee to someone working a long shift: a nurse, a security guard, a night clerk you know.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 292, 'Ask a family member to walk you through an old family photo album, in person or on a video call.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 293, 'Let someone at work know you are free to help if their week gets heavy.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 294, 'Ask a friend to join you for the first day of a new season: the first swim, the first snow, the first cider.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 295, 'Send a message that asks nothing and simply shares something good from your day.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 296, 'Ask someone new at work, school, or your building if they have found their way around yet.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 297, 'Cheer for a friend''s team, race, or performance by showing up in person if you can.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 298, 'Ask a longtime friend what has changed about you since you first met.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 299, 'Bring a friend along to a volunteer shift, a clean-up, or a food drive.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 300, 'Snap a photo of a book cover and ask a friend if they have read it.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 301, 'Carpool, walk, or ride to work with a coworker once this week.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 302, 'Tell a friend one way they have changed for the better since you met.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 303, 'Set a standing lunch date with a coworker: same day, same place, every other week.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 304, 'Ask the host of a party or event if there is anything you can do to help, and stay in the kitchen with them.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 305, 'Send a friend a movie or show suggestion and pick a night to watch it together, in person or apart.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 306, 'Talk to a teenager or young adult in your family about what they are into right now.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 307, 'Follow up in a week on something a friend is working through, and tell them now that you will.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 308, 'Invite a new coworker or classmate to sit with your group at lunch.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 309, 'Call a friend on a long drive and let the miles pass in conversation.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 310, 'Ask a neighbor about a holiday decoration, a flag, or a sign in their yard.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 311, 'Reconnect with someone from a wedding party, a team, or a trip group you were in together.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 312, 'Find out what a friend is dreading this week and offer to help or just listen.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 313, 'Say something friendly to the person you always see walking a dog at the same time as you.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 314, 'Tell a friend about a place you went this week and ask if they want to go next time.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 315, 'Find out from a family member what they were doing at your age.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 316, 'Go to a trivia night, open mic, or game night with one friend and talk to another table.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 317, 'Message a friend who is far away with a photo of the sky where you are, and ask for one back.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 318, 'Find out what a coworker is proud of from this month.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 319, 'Send a quick "I saw this and thought of you" to a family member, not just a friend.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 320, 'Learn a phrase in a language a friend speaks by asking them to teach it to you.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 321, 'Invite your neighbors over for a simple porch, stoop, or yard hour with lemonade or cider.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 322, 'Ask an older friend or relative what advice they would give their younger self.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 323, 'Tell a friend about a habit you are trying to start and ask if they will check in on you.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 324, 'Find one person at a work event or a party who looks alone and start with a question.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 325, 'Ask a friend to swap a book, a game, or a piece of gear with you for a month.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 326, 'End your next message to a friend with a real question, so they have something to answer.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 327, 'Trade favorite photos from this year with a family member.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 328, 'Take a walk with a coworker instead of a coffee break, and let the conversation wander.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 329, 'Check how a friend is handling the holidays, the heat, or the cold, whatever the season brings.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 330, 'Call someone on their birthday instead of posting on their page.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 331, 'Plan a piece of a friend''s ideal weekend with them, after asking what it looks like.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 332, 'Photograph a sunset, a first snow, or a blooming tree and send it to someone with a note that it made you think of them.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 333, 'Ask a coworker to tell you about the best boss or teacher they ever had.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 334, 'Keep a small list of things friends mention, then ask about one the next time you talk.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 335, 'Offer to split a bulk order, a delivery, or a seasonal chore with a neighbor.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 336, 'Name an opinion of a friend''s that changed your mind, and tell them so.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 337, 'Swap childhood favorite books with a friend, or ask what they read to their kids, and share yours.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 338, 'Write a thank-you note to a coach, a teacher, or a boss from long ago and send it.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 339, 'Turn a hardware store, nursery, or big-box run into a hangout by bringing a friend along for the project.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 340, 'Invite a friend to a morning walk before work or school, even once.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 341, 'Ask someone at your place of worship, gym, or club to tell you how they first came there.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 342, 'Message a friend who is sick to ask what they need, and offer something specific.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 343, 'Ask your partner or closest friend what they would like more of from you.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 344, 'Send a friend a note on the last day of the year about one thing you shared in it.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 345, 'Ask a friend to try a new recipe with you, in one kitchen or two, on a video call.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 346, 'Tell a coworker you noticed they seemed off this week and ask if they want to talk.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 347, 'Ask a family member to teach you something they know how to do: a stitch, a repair, a card trick.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 348, 'Send a photo of a place from your shared past to a sibling or cousin, and ask what they remember.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 349, 'Ask a friend to meet for breakfast instead of dinner, and see how different the conversation feels.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 350, 'Talk to the person next to you on a plane, a train, or a bus for at least a few minutes.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 351, 'Ask a coworker to grab lunch together on a Friday and leave work talk at the door.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 352, 'Send a friend a reminder of a promise you made each other, and ask if they still want to keep it.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 353, 'Ask a neighbor to join you for a walk to the polling place, the park, or the farmers market.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 354, 'Tell a friend the thing you have been meaning to say and keep putting off, in a message or in person.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 355, 'Ask a family member which relative you remind them of and why.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 356, 'Time a message to a friend in another time zone so it lands in their morning.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 357, 'Visit a museum, a garden, or an exhibit with a friend this month.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 358, 'Reach out to someone from a support group, a class, or a program you once attended.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 359, 'Ask a coworker what they do to unwind after work.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 360, 'Tell a friend that you are around and free on a specific evening this week, and see who takes you up on it.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 361, 'Ask the person who delivers your mail or packages how their route is going.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 362, 'Remind a friend that you are thinking of them during a season they find hard.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 363, 'Swap podcast episode recommendations with a friend and talk about them once you have both listened.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 364, 'Sit near someone at a coffee shop and say one thing, about the weather, the line, the music.'),
  ('reaching-out-to-people', 365, 'Pick one person from this year of reaching out and tell them what their company has meant to you.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 1, 'Set a fifteen-minute "worry window" this evening. When worries appear earlier, write them down and save them for then.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 2, 'Write down one worry and sort it: something you can act on, or something you cannot. Act on the first kind, breathe through the second.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 3, 'Notice one "what if" today and answer it with "even if that happened, I would..."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 4, 'Take a worry and write down the most likely outcome, not the worst one.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 5, 'Ask yourself: "Is this worry solving anything right now?" If not, put it down for an hour.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 6, 'Do something with your hands for ten minutes, cooking, gardening, drawing, and let your mind follow.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 7, 'Write down a worry from last month. Did it come true? What actually happened?'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 8, 'When you catch yourself worrying, name what you can see, hear, and feel right now.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 9, 'Pick one small step on the thing you are worried about and do it today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 10, 'Limit checking the news to two set times today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 11, 'Tell someone one worry out loud. Notice how it changes when it is said.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 12, 'Breathe out for longer than you breathe in, ten times, when a worry spikes.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 13, 'Write a worry on paper, fold it, and put it in a drawer until tomorrow.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 14, 'Notice a worry about someone else and ask whether there is something kind you could do for them instead.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 15, 'Spend ten minutes on something that fully absorbs you, a puzzle, a game, a craft.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 16, 'Ask: "What would I tell a friend who was worrying about this?" and take your own advice.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 17, 'Rate a worry from zero to ten in the morning and again at night. Notice the difference.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 18, 'Replace one "I can''t stop thinking about it" with "I am choosing to think about something else for now."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 19, 'Make a short list of what is going fine today. Worry tends to leave those off.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 20, 'Delay checking for a reply or result by thirty minutes today and see what happens in the gap.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 21, 'Write down the thing you are worried about and next to it the date you will actually know the answer.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 22, 'Do a quick body check: unclench your jaw, drop your shoulders, loosen your hands.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 23, 'Write down what you would do if the worst case happened, in three steps. Having a plan shrinks it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 24, 'Spend fifteen minutes outside and leave the worry indoors.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 25, 'Notice a worry that is really about wanting certainty. Say, "I can handle not knowing for now."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 26, 'Choose one worry to stop researching online today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 27, 'Say to a worry: "Thanks for trying to protect me. I have got this."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 28, 'Make a small decision you have been putting off, in under two minutes.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 29, 'Look at your worry notes from this challenge and count how many worries came true. Let the number speak.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 30, 'Write down one thing you want to do this week that worry has been talking you out of, and do the first step.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 31, 'Before you get out of bed, name the one worry waiting for you and tell it, "Not yet, we will meet at seven tonight."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 32, 'Keep a small notebook in your pocket today and jot each worry as it arrives, without solving any of them until dinner.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 33, 'Choose a worry that has been circling for days and ask a simple question: "What is the one fact I am missing?" Go find that fact.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 34, 'Set a timer for five minutes and worry on purpose, as hard as you can. When it rings, stop and make a cup of tea.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 35, 'Write a worry as a headline, then write the boring version of the story that most likely follows it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 36, 'On your commute, count the worries that show up and give each one a number instead of a reply.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 37, 'Pick the worry that costs you the most sleep and write down who could actually give you an answer. Contact them today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 38, 'Move your worry window to your lunch break today and see whether a daytime slot works better than an evening one.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 39, 'Notice a worry that begins with "I should have" and ask whether there is anything left to do about it now. If not, close the file.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 40, 'When a worry arrives while you are working, type it into a note, close the note, and return to the task in front of you.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 41, 'Take one worry about money and turn it into a single number you can check, a balance, a bill, a date. Check it, then stop.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 42, 'Send the email, make the call, or fill out the form you have been worrying about instead of doing. Ten minutes is enough.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 43, 'Ask a worry, "What is the smallest version of this problem?" and deal with that version today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 44, 'Walk around the block once and let every worry that comes up ride along without answering it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 45, 'Write a worry in pencil and, next to it, in pen, one thing you know for certain about the situation.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 46, 'Tell a worry, "You can come back at the worry window," and say it out loud if you are alone.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 47, 'Spot a worry about tomorrow and do one small thing tonight that makes tomorrow easier: lay out clothes, pack a bag, set an alarm.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 48, 'Ask someone you trust to hold a worry for you today. Say, "I just need to hand this to you for the afternoon."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 49, 'When a worry says "what if it goes wrong," add "and what if it goes fine?" and sit with both for a minute.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 50, 'Look at a worry and mark it with a letter: A for act, W for wait, L for let go. Do only what the letter says.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 51, 'Give a persistent worry a name, like a weather system, and note when it passes through today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 52, 'Take a photo of the thing you are worried about, a bill, a message, a calendar, and close the app. It is saved; you do not need to hold it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 53, 'Write down three worries and cross out the two you cannot do anything about this week.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 54, 'Choose one thing you keep checking, a tracker, an inbox, a bank app, and check it once today, at a time you pick in advance.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 55, 'Before a meeting or appointment, write down what you are worried will happen. Afterward, write what did.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 56, 'Notice the moment a worry turns into a plan. Write the plan down and let the worry retire.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 57, 'Wash the dishes slowly and let each worry go down the drain with the water.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 58, 'Write down the question a worry keeps asking and answer it with "I will find out on" and a date, then put the pen down.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 59, 'Take a worry that is about being late and leave ten minutes earlier instead of thinking about it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 60, 'Read a chapter of a book at lunch instead of rehearsing the afternoon.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 61, 'Write a worry on a sticky note and stick it to the fridge. It stays there, you go about your day.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 62, 'Pick a worry about your health and book the appointment or make the call that would settle it, rather than reading about it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 63, 'Sit outside for five minutes at sunset and say to yourself, "Whatever I am worried about, it will still be there in the morning, and so will I."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 64, 'Before bed, write tomorrow''s to-do list so your worries have somewhere to sleep other than your head.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 65, 'Ask yourself whether a worry belongs to today, this week, or someday. Only today''s worries get your attention now.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 66, 'Spot an old worry wearing new clothes. Write down the first time you had it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 67, 'Call or text the person you are worried about instead of guessing how they are.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 68, 'Hold a warm drink and, for each sip, name one worry you are choosing to leave alone until later.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 69, 'Find the smallest fact that would shrink a worry and go find it: a train time, a price, a due date.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 70, 'Write down what a worry wants you to do and what you would rather do. Do the second one.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 71, 'Turn a "what if" into a "when," if it is truly likely, and write down the first step you would take.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 72, 'Ask a coworker how they handle a shared uncertainty. Borrow one of their tricks today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 73, 'Spend a full minute noticing what your body does when a worry arrives, then let your shoulders drop.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 74, 'Give yourself permission to not know something today. Say it plainly: "I do not know yet, and that is allowed."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 75, 'Take one worry and write the best-case outcome, the worst-case outcome, and the most likely one. Circle the last.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 76, 'Set a "no worry zone" for one room of your home today. Worries wait at the door.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 77, 'Try holding a worry in one hand as if it were a small stone. Open your hand and set it on the table.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 78, 'Listen to a full song with your eyes closed and give the worry that comes up the length of the song, then no more.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 79, 'Ask a worry, "Whose job is this?" If it is not yours, hand it back in your mind.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 80, 'Write a worry as a text you would never send, then delete it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 81, 'Do the chore you have been avoiding because worrying about it felt easier than starting.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 82, 'Look up the one thing that would resolve a worry for good, then close the browser and do not open a second tab.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 83, 'Ask a worry to wait until you have eaten. Have a proper meal, then see whether it is still as loud.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 84, 'Say to yourself, "I have handled unknown things before," and name one you handled.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 85, 'Split a big worry into three small questions. Answer only the one you can answer today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 86, 'Notice if you are worrying to feel prepared. Then do one actual preparation instead, like writing a list or checking a map.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 87, 'Choose an evening activity that requires your hands and eyes, a jigsaw, kneading dough, sorting photos, and give worry the night off.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 88, 'Write down a worry, then write "so what?" underneath, and answer honestly.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 89, 'Ask a friend to tell you about their week before you tell them about your worry. Notice whether it shrinks while you listen.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 90, 'Rate how urgent a worry feels, then rate how urgent it actually is. Act on the second number.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 91, 'Put your phone in another room for one hour this evening and let the worries that need it wait.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 92, 'Write one sentence about what you will do if the thing you fear happens, then one about what you will do if it does not.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 93, 'Tackle the paperwork, the renewal, or the appointment that a worry keeps pointing at. Fifteen minutes, then stop.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 94, 'Take a worry to the shower with you and let it stay there when you step out.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 95, 'Draw a circle and write inside it what you control about a worry. Write the rest outside the circle. Only work inside.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 96, 'When a worry is about someone''s opinion, ask whether they have ever said it. If not, file it under "guess."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 97, 'Notice one worry you have carried for over a year. Ask whether it has earned that much of your time.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 98, 'Plant something, a seed, a bulb, a cutting, and let the waiting be practice for the other things you are waiting on.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 99, 'Tell a worry, "I will give you five minutes at four o''clock," then keep the appointment and keep it short.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 100, 'Write down the worry that showed up most this week and one thing you learned about it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 101, 'Start the morning by writing a worry on the back of a receipt and leaving it in your coat pocket until you get home.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 102, 'While the coffee brews, tell yourself which worry gets the first ten minutes tonight and which ones do not make the cut.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 103, 'On a walk today, every time a worry appears, name a tree, a car, or a shop you pass instead, and keep walking.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 104, 'Text someone "How are you?" before worrying about whether they are upset with you.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 105, 'Take one worry about your job and write down the single question you could ask your manager to settle it. Ask it this week.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 106, 'Open the letter, message, or statement you have been avoiding. Read it once and note what, if anything, needs doing.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 107, 'Sort today''s worries into two columns, "mine" and "not mine," and give the second column back.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 108, 'Do a ten-minute tidy of one surface and let your mind file a worry away while your hands file the mess.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 109, 'Give a worry the last word only after you have said, "I will decide about this on Friday."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 110, 'Swap ten minutes of reading about a worry for ten minutes of a cookbook, a comic, or a field guide.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 111, 'Before you check your phone this morning, write down what you are afraid it will say. Then look.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 112, 'Ask an older relative or friend what they used to worry about at your age, and what came of it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 113, 'Pick one worry and write a tiny experiment to test it: ask, look, try. Run it before the end of the day.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 114, 'When a worry comes up at your desk, stand, stretch, refill your water, and sit back down to the task, not the worry.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 115, 'Write a worry at the top of a page and underneath list the people who would help if it came true.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 116, 'Schedule a worry for the weekend and write it on the calendar so your weekday self can trust it will be handled.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 117, 'Notice a worry that gets louder at night. Tell it you will look at it in daylight, when it is usually smaller.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 118, 'Cook something that needs stirring and let the stirring be the only thing you have to keep track of.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 119, 'Make a list of what you would need to know to stop worrying about one thing. Cross off what is unknowable.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 120, 'Take a worry about a conversation and write your opening sentence. Having the first line makes the rest easier.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 121, 'Ask yourself what a calm person who knew all the facts would do about this worry today, then do that one thing.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 122, 'Turn a worry into a checklist of three items. Check the first one off before lunch.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 123, 'Sit on a bench outside for ten minutes and let the worries pass like traffic. You are not the road.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 124, 'Write one worry in the past tense, as if it is already over, and see how you feel reading it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 125, 'Notice how a worry sounds when you say it slowly, out loud, in an empty room.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 126, 'Delay reading the news until after breakfast and see whether the morning goes any differently.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 127, 'Draw a quick map of a worry: the fear in the middle, the facts around it. Look at how much of the page is fact.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 128, 'Pay one bill, renew one thing, or cancel one subscription that a worry keeps tapping you about.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 129, 'Spend five minutes at the end of work writing down what you are leaving unfinished, so it does not come home with you.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 130, 'Compare a worry with the last three times you had it. Write down how those three ended.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 131, 'Water the plants and, while you do, decide which worry is getting no water from you today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 132, 'Look at your calendar and find the date by which one worry will resolve itself. Write "answer arrives" on that day.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 133, 'Say "maybe" to a worry instead of "yes" or "no," then get on with your afternoon.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 134, 'Set a two-minute timer and clear your desk, your bag, or your car. A cleared space asks less of a worried mind.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 135, 'Ask a partner, friend, or roommate to be your "worry parking attendant" tonight. Hand them the ticket and pick it up tomorrow.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 136, 'Choose one worry and find out its actual deadline. Most have one further away than the mind claims.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 137, 'Give yourself a bedtime rule: worries after lights out go on the pad by the bed, not into your head.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 138, 'Notice when a worry is really about being tired. Go to bed half an hour earlier instead of thinking about it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 139, 'Make the phone call you have been dreading, and time how long it actually takes.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 140, 'Before a trip, write a packing list instead of running through everything that could go wrong on the way.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 141, 'Jot down a worry and, beside it, who else is carrying it. Share the load with them today, even in a sentence.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 142, 'Take one worry and imagine explaining it to a ten-year-old. Notice which parts you cannot make sound serious.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 143, 'Put a chair by a window and give a worry ten minutes of your full attention there. When you stand up, it stays in the chair.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 144, 'Sweep the porch, the steps, or the hallway, and let the rhythm carry a worry out with the dust.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 145, 'Write down what you will do first thing tomorrow about a worry, then close the notebook for the night.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 146, 'Spend your lunch break away from screens and give each worry that comes along a nod, but not a seat.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 147, 'Ask a worry, "Is there a phone number, a form, or a person that would settle this?" and start there.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 148, 'Note one worry that vanished on its own this month without your help. Let that count as evidence.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 149, 'Fold laundry and, with each item, set down one small worry you have been carrying since morning.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 150, 'Name the three things that are most likely to happen tomorrow. Notice how ordinary they are.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 151, 'Pick a worry that is about a decision and give yourself a deadline to decide. Write the deadline where you will see it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 152, 'Wear something comfortable today and notice whether a relaxed body makes worry a little quieter.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 153, 'Turn off notifications for one app that feeds a worry, just for today, and see what changes.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 154, 'Take a worry to a friend and ask only one thing: "Have you ever had this one?"'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 155, 'Write down what you are worried about in one sentence, and what you are actually going to do about it in one sentence. Do the second.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 156, 'Before you fall asleep, list three things that went fine today that you worried about this morning.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 157, 'Go for a bike ride, a swim, or a long walk and leave your phone behind for the length of it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 158, 'Take the first step on a project a worry has been guarding: open the file, buy the paint, email the person.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 159, 'Say to a worry, "You are a guess," and write down what would make it a fact.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 160, 'Choose a worry that has a yes or no answer and ask the question today, even if the answer might be no.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 161, 'Watch clouds, a fire, or a fish tank for five minutes and let a worry drift by at the same speed.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 162, 'Practice saying "I will find out when I find out" to one worry that cannot be answered today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 163, 'Spend the last ten minutes of your workday writing tomorrow''s plan, so the evening belongs to you.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 164, 'Set a limit of one search on a worrying topic today. After that, the browser stays closed.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 165, 'Write down a worry that is really a wish for someone to be okay. Do one kind thing for them today instead.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 166, 'Take a worry and imagine it a year from now. Write down whether you think you will remember it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 167, 'Fix the small thing that a worry keeps pointing at: the loose handle, the flat tire, the unread form.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 168, 'Try worrying in the third person, "she is worried that," and notice whether it loosens the grip.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 169, 'Take a nap, a stretch, or a snack before deciding whether a worry deserves attention. Bodies exaggerate when tired.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 170, 'Book the thing you have been putting off, the dentist, the oil change, the checkup, and let the booking do the worrying.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 171, 'Open the blinds first thing and let the morning light in before you let the first worry in.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 172, 'On a cold morning, warm your hands on a mug and decide which worry is allowed to come to work with you. Only one.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 173, 'Write a worry on the steamed-up bathroom mirror and watch it fade as the room clears.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 174, 'Rake leaves, shovel snow, or pull weeds for fifteen minutes and let the effort do what the worrying was pretending to do.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 175, 'Ask yourself at noon: "Which worry has had the most airtime today?" Give it five minutes, then change the channel.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 176, 'Write down one worry about a child, a parent, or a pet, and one practical thing you can do for them this week.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 177, 'Take a worry about being judged and write down the last time someone actually judged you for it. Look at how long ago it was.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 178, 'Text a friend a photo of something ordinary instead of a message about what you are worried about.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 179, 'Give a worry a shelf. Say, "This goes on the shelf until Saturday," and put it there each time it climbs down.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 180, 'Set out tomorrow''s breakfast tonight, so one small unknown is already known.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 181, 'Try a new route to work or the store and let the unfamiliar streets take the attention a worry usually gets.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 182, 'Ask a worry whether it is about the past, the present, or the future. Only present ones get a response today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 183, 'Check one worry against a calendar: is there actually a date for this, or has your mind invented urgency?'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 184, 'Write down the most boring possible explanation for something that is worrying you. Boring is often right.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 185, 'Do one thing at a time this afternoon and notice whether a worry has less room when you are not juggling.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 186, 'Say "not now" to a worry three times today and follow through each time by turning to a task.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 187, 'Write a worry a short letter: "Dear worry, I have heard you. I will review your case at seven." Sign it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 188, 'Take a long, slow walk after dinner and give a worry until the first street corner. After that, it walks in silence.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 189, 'Before a doctor''s appointment or a review, write your three questions. Prepared people worry less on the drive.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 190, 'Spend ten minutes on a hobby that has nothing to do with anything you are worried about.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 191, 'Leave the worry about what to cook by choosing tonight''s dinner now, in one minute, and moving on.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 192, 'Take a worry about a friend''s silence and send a light message. Most silences are busy, not angry.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 193, 'Write down which worry you would keep if you could only keep one. Let the others go for the day.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 194, 'Turn a worry into a question you can ask a professional, a plumber, a pharmacist, a bank, and ask it today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 195, 'Pick a worry and find out what would happen if you simply did nothing about it for a week.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 196, 'Say out loud what you would be doing right now if you were not worrying. Do ten minutes of that.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 197, 'Try a "worry walk" this weekend: walk and worry for the first half, walk and notice for the second half.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 198, 'Write down three worries and, next to each, whether it has a form, a call, or a wait attached. Do the forms.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 199, 'Choose a worry about an outcome and write down what you will do the day after, whichever way it goes.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 200, 'Notice when a worry pulls you to reread a message. Read it once more, then archive it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 201, 'Sit at the kitchen table for five minutes with a worry and a piece of fruit. Eat the fruit. Leave the worry.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 202, 'Sing or hum on the drive home and let a worry find out it cannot compete with a chorus.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 203, 'Set a rule for today: worries are allowed, but only in writing.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 204, 'Give one worry a nickname and say, "Oh, it is you again," when it appears.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 205, 'Ask a worry, "What would I do differently today if I already knew the answer?" and do that.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 206, 'Take one worry about the future and write what is true about it today. Only today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 207, 'Spend an hour offline this evening and let the worries that need a screen wait for tomorrow.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 208, 'Choose a repeating worry and count how many times it shows up before lunch. Then let the count be enough.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 209, 'Write down what you would pay to have a worry answered, then notice you already have the time to find out for free.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 210, 'Notice a worry about a deadline and check the deadline. If it is real, do fifteen minutes on it. If it is not, note the real date.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 211, 'Take a worry about money and make one small move: transfer a few dollars, cancel a trial, check a rate.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 212, 'Spend a few minutes with a pet, a plant, or a view, and let a worry watch from the sidelines.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 213, 'Ask a worry, "Are you helping me prepare or just helping me feel busy?" and act on the honest answer.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 214, 'Make a note of one thing you were worried about at this time last year. Write down how it turned out.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 215, 'Stand in the doorway before leaving home and say, "Whatever happens today, I will handle it at the time."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 216, 'When a worry says "everyone will notice," ask who "everyone" is. Write down the actual names, if any.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 217, 'Bake something simple and let the timer do the waiting so you do not have to.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 218, 'Write down a worry about someone else''s choice and remind yourself which choices are theirs to make.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 219, 'Pick a task you have been circling and give it the first twenty minutes of your morning, before any worry can argue.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 220, 'Change one worrying thought into a scheduling decision: "I will think about this at three, for ten minutes."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 221, 'Take a worry about the weather, the traffic, or the delay and write what you will do if it happens. Then check the forecast once.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 222, 'Read a poem or a short story before bed rather than your worry list.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 223, 'Try a slow evening stretch and, with each breath out, let one worry loosen its hold.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 224, 'Go through your worry notes and highlight the ones that were answered by simply waiting.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 225, 'Ask someone to tell you the most likely outcome of a worry. Outsiders are often better at odds.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 226, 'Notice a worry that comes with a "should" and change it to "I am choosing to," or drop it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 227, 'Write on a card, "I do not have to solve this today," and carry it in your wallet.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 228, 'Spend the first five minutes at your desk on one concrete task, not on checking anything.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 229, 'Take one worry to the gym, the pool, or a trail and let it try to keep up.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 230, 'Say to a worry, "I will believe you when you bring evidence," and get on with your day.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 231, 'Draft the difficult message you have been worrying about, then leave it in drafts until tomorrow. Drafting is doing.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 232, 'Sort your worries by size, pebble, rock, boulder, and carry only the pebbles today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 233, 'Look around the room and name three things that are working: the lights, the heat, the door that locks.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 234, 'Ask a worry whether it would still be a worry if you had slept nine hours. If not, plan for the sleep.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 235, 'Spend ten minutes learning something new and unrelated, a word, a knot, a chord, and give the worry no room to sit.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 236, 'Write down a worry as a to-do instead: not "what if the car breaks down" but "book the service."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 237, 'Give yourself a "done for today" time and, when it arrives, tell any worry that shows up that the office is closed.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 238, 'Wake up and, before anything else, write down the worry that arrived overnight. Then decide whether it gets any daylight.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 239, 'Pack your lunch or your bag the night before and take one "did I forget" off tomorrow morning''s list.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 240, 'Take a worry about a test result, a grade, or a verdict and write down the two most likely responses you would have. Pick which one you would rather practice.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 241, 'Spend five minutes in a park, a yard, or a parking lot with trees, and give your worry to the wind for that long.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 242, 'Ask a worry to show you its receipt. What has it ever bought you? Write the honest answer.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 243, 'Tell a coworker one small thing you are unsure about and ask what they would do. Sharing the unknown halves it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 244, 'Hand-write a worry in the largest letters you can, then in the smallest. Notice which size feels truer.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 245, 'Delete one app, bookmark, or feed that keeps handing you fresh things to worry about.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 246, 'Do the task you are worried about badly on purpose, just a first draft, and see whether the worry had anything left to say.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 247, 'Take a worry about a relationship and say one honest sentence to the person instead of guessing for another day.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 248, 'Give a worry a color and picture it fading a shade every time you choose to do something else.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 249, 'Write down what you would tell your younger self about the thing you are worried about now.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 250, 'Set a "check-in" not a "check": look at the thing you are worried about once, note the status, and close it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 251, 'Make your bed slowly and let the flattened sheets be your signal that today''s worry is smoothed out too.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 252, 'Notice a worry that sounds like a family member''s voice. Ask whether it is yours to keep.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 253, 'Try answering a worry with "we will see," and let the phrase be a complete sentence.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 254, 'Do a chore outdoors, washing the car, sweeping the walk, clearing gutters, and let the air take some of the worry.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 255, 'Take one worry and write down what "good enough" would look like. Aim for that, not for certainty.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 256, 'Let a worry wait until you have finished a page, a task, or a walk. Then ask it to wait again.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 257, 'Spend the ride home listening to a podcast about something you know nothing about.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 258, 'Write down the person you would call if the thing you worry about happened. Notice you already have a first step.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 259, 'Notice a worry that is asking you to control someone else. Choose one thing you can do for yourself instead.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 260, 'Finish something small today, a form, a drawer, a reply, and let "finished" be louder than "what if."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 261, 'Take a worry and ask, "What is the next right thing?" Do only the next one.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 262, 'Sit in the car for one minute before going inside and leave the day''s worries in the passenger seat.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 263, 'Write a worry as a weather report: "Cloudy with a chance of overthinking." Then check what the sky is actually doing.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 264, 'Choose one worry that always comes with a reread. Today, read the message once and answer it instead.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 265, 'Ask yourself what you would do this weekend if you were not worrying. Put one of those things on the calendar.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 266, 'Eat lunch away from your desk and let the worry stay with the keyboard.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 267, 'Take a worry about a mistake you made and write the sentence you would say to apologize or fix it. Say it if it fits.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 268, 'Write the date on a worry, and set a reminder to reread it in a month.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 269, 'Notice a worry that starts with "what will they think" and answer, "They are mostly thinking about themselves."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 270, 'Give a worry exactly three sentences on paper, no more. Fold the page in half when you reach the third.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 271, 'Do something slightly brave that a worry has been steering you away from: speak first, sit in the front row, ask the question.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 272, 'Buy the groceries, fill the tank, or top up the account you keep worrying about running out.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 273, 'Spend a few minutes on a windowsill, a stoop, or a balcony and give a worry the same attention you give the pigeons.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 274, 'Put a price on finding out: ask a worry what it would cost to know. If it is a phone call, pay it today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 275, 'Write a worry on your hand in the morning and wash it off after lunch, whether or not it has been solved.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 276, 'Notice a worry that peaks on Sunday evening. Put one nice thing in Monday morning so it has less to say.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 277, 'Try saying "I am worried, and I am also going to make dinner," and then make dinner.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 278, 'Choose the worry that interrupts you most at work and give it a scheduled slot in your calendar, with an end time.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 279, 'Do a sudoku, a crossword, or a word game over coffee and let a worry sit out one round.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 280, 'Take a worry about aging, yours or someone else''s, and do one small act of care today instead of forecasting.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 281, 'List what worries you and what you are grateful for, side by side. Read the right column twice.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 282, 'Ask a worry, "Would I want a friend to spend their evening on this?" If not, spend yours on something else.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 283, 'Spend ten minutes clearing out a bag, a drawer, or an inbox and notice which worries were attached to old things.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 284, 'Say "that is a tomorrow problem" out loud to one worry, and mean it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 285, 'Take a worry about someone''s safety and send a simple "thinking of you." Then trust them with their own day.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 286, 'Practice waiting: stand in the longest checkout line on purpose and notice the worry you would usually fill it with.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 287, 'Write a worry, then write what you would need to see in order to be ninety percent sure it will not happen. Go check for that.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 288, 'Give a worry a run: jog, march, or walk fast for ten minutes and see how much of it is left when you stop.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 289, 'Before a family gathering, write down the one thing you are worried someone will say. Then write your calm reply.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 290, 'Take a worry about being enough and list three things you did today that were, in fact, enough.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 291, 'Turn a "what if I fail" into "what if I try," and take the first step within the hour.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 292, 'Sit with your back to your desk for two minutes and give your eyes a worry-free view.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 293, 'Write down one worry you have never said out loud, then say it to one person you trust today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 294, 'Notice a worry that has a "should have by now" attached. Cross out "by now."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 295, 'Choose one worry to hand to your future self. Write, "Future me will handle this on" and a date. Then trust them.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 296, 'Take a worry about the house and do one repair, one call, or one measurement toward it today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 297, 'Spend the first hour of a day off without checking anything. Let the worries find out you are not available.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 298, 'Write a worry as a "maybe" and its opposite as a "maybe" too. Hold both for the day.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 299, 'Ask a worry, "Is this a two-minute thing?" If it is, do it now and let the worry go with it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 300, 'Take a worry about the future of your work and update one thing today: a resume line, a skill, a contact.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 301, 'Do one small favor for a neighbor and notice whether your worry had to wait while you did it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 302, 'Write "answer pending" on a worry and stop trying to write the answer yourself.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 303, 'Set the table, light a candle, or put on music for dinner and give the evening a shape that worry has to fit around.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 304, 'Notice one worry that dissolves when you say it to another person. Keep a list of those.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 305, 'Say to yourself in the mirror, "I can worry later, and I probably will not need to," and leave the bathroom.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 306, 'Start the day with a stretch by the window and tell the first worry you spot, "Later, and in writing."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 307, 'Take a worry about a trip, a move, or a change and do one concrete thing toward it: a list, a booking, a box.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 308, 'Try describing a worry as if it were a small animal you found on the path. Notice it, step around it, keep walking.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 309, 'Write down a worry that you have already solved once. Reread your old solution and reuse it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 310, 'Ask a worry to name a date. If it cannot, it does not get a spot on your calendar today.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 311, 'Spend fifteen minutes doing something generous, a note, a delivery, a call, and let worry find the door locked.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 312, 'Notice one worry that is about wanting to be liked. Do something you like instead, for ten minutes.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 313, 'Wash your face with cold water and say, "That is enough of that one," to the worry you have been holding since breakfast.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 314, 'Choose a worry to put in a jar, literally, on a slip of paper. Empty the jar at the end of the season and read what came true.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 315, 'Revisit a conversation that still worries you and write what you would say if you got a second chance. Then decide if you need one.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 316, 'Try worrying only while standing today. Sit down, and the worry has to wait.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 317, 'Give one worry a "consult": ask an expert, read one reliable page, and then stop collecting opinions.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 318, 'Write down what you will not do about a worry today, and let "not doing" be a decision rather than an accident.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 319, 'Take a worry to a body of water, a river, a pond, a fountain, and let the water carry your attention for five minutes.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 320, 'Ask yourself what a worry wants you to avoid, then do a tiny version of that thing.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 321, 'Send the thank-you, the RSVP, or the follow-up you have been worrying about being late with. Late is better than never, and it is done.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 322, 'Take a worry about a child''s future and do one thing with them today that has nothing to do with the future.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 323, 'Try a "worry swap" with a friend: each of you names one, and you talk about the other person''s, not your own.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 324, 'Write down one worry as a question to a stranger on a bus. Notice how odd it sounds when it leaves your head.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 325, 'Do a slow loop of your home and touch three things that are fine: the locked door, the full fridge, the working faucet.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 326, 'Give a worry a "seat" in the room, a chair or a cushion, and speak to it there, briefly, then leave the room.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 327, 'Ask a worry what it would say if it were kind. Write that version down and read it instead.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 328, 'Make one decision today without checking with anyone, and let the worry about being wrong come along for the ride.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 329, 'Water a garden, a lawn, or a windowsill and let a worry wait for the can to empty.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 330, 'If a friend''s health worries you, ask them directly how they are, rather than reading between lines.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 331, 'Write on a slip of paper, "This will be answered by" and a date. Tape it to the mirror and stop rewriting the ending.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 332, 'Spend a rainy hour indoors with a project that needs your hands more than your head.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 333, 'Notice a worry that arrives in the shower or the car, places you cannot act. Say, "I will look at you when I have hands and a desk."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 334, 'Take a worry about a purchase and sleep on it. If it still matters tomorrow, decide then.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 335, 'Try one hour of "single-tasking" this afternoon and notice whether worry has fewer gaps to slip into.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 336, 'Take a worry about the past and write down the one thing you would do differently. Then write, "I did not know that then."'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 337, 'Set a timer for two minutes and list everything that is not wrong right now. Keep the list nearby.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 338, 'Give a worry to a walk with a dog, a friend, or a podcast, and see how much of it makes it home.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 339, 'Write down one worry that a good night''s sleep would shrink. Go to bed at a reasonable hour tonight and check in the morning.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 340, 'Ask a worry to prove it with one fact. Give it thirty seconds. If nothing comes, move on.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 341, 'Choose a worry about a gathering and write your exit plan. Knowing you can leave makes staying easier.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 342, 'Take a worry about a bill and call the company. Most have a plan, a date, or an answer.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 343, 'Try a "worry-free hour" with a friend or partner and agree to talk about anything else.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 344, 'Plan tonight''s replacement for worrying, in writing. Be specific: a show, a bath, a chapter, a call.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 345, 'Take a worry about a loud world and turn the volume down, literally, for an hour: no radio, no notifications, no news.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 346, 'Do the thing a worry says is too hard for five minutes, then decide whether to keep going.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 347, 'Write down the biggest worry of the month and one small thing you are proud of doing about it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 348, 'Try telling a worry, "You are welcome to stay, but I am going to the store," and go to the store.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 349, 'Take a worry about being behind and write down where you actually are. Compare with the finish line, not with someone else.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 350, 'Ask a worry, "Who is this really for?" If it is for someone else, do them a favor rather than a forecast.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 351, 'Take a worry outside on a clear night and look up for a full minute. Notice how far away it feels from up there.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 352, 'Choose the worry you would most like to retire and write its retirement date. Mark the day with something small.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 353, 'Write your worries on a whiteboard or a big page and erase one each time you act on it, wait on it, or let it go.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 354, 'Say "not today" to one worry and "yes, today" to one task. Do the task.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 355, 'Spend the last five minutes of the day writing what tomorrow''s first step is. Nothing else goes on the page.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 356, 'Take a worry about an apology you owe and make it, simply, in one sentence.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 357, 'Sit with a warm meal and give a worry the length of the meal. Then clear the table, and the worry with it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 358, 'Try a "sounds like" for one worry: "That sounds like the one about not being ready." Naming the pattern loosens it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 359, 'Take one worry and imagine handing it to a very calm person. Write what they would do first, then do that.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 360, 'Go through your worry notes from this challenge and pick the one tool you will keep using after it ends.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 361, 'Let the last worry of the day be written, not thought. Then close the notebook and turn out the light.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 362, 'Write down what a year of setting worry down has taught you, in three sentences, and keep the page where you will find it again.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 363, 'Spend five minutes at a window or a doorway watching people or weather go by, and let a worry go by with them.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 364, 'Take a worry about the season ahead, the holidays, the heat, the dark, and plan one thing you will enjoy in it.'),
  ('loosening-the-grip-of-worry', 365, 'Try listing what you know for certain about a worry. Read the list twice, then go do the next ordinary thing.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 1, 'Write down one thing you agreed to recently that you did not want to do.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 2, 'Say "Let me check and get back to you" to one request today instead of answering right away.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 3, 'Notice one moment today when your body tightened. That is often a boundary being crossed.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 4, 'Practice saying "No, I can''t do that" out loud, alone, five times.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 5, 'Turn down one small thing today, an extra task, a call, a favor, with one sentence and no apology.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 6, 'Decide on a time to stop working today and stop at that time.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 7, 'Write down three things you need more of: time, quiet, help, rest, and one way to get one of them.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 8, 'Tell someone what you would prefer, instead of going along with their plan.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 9, 'Leave one message unanswered until tomorrow. Nothing will break.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 10, 'Say "I am not available then, but I could do Thursday" to one request.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 11, 'Notice one time you over-explained yourself today and practice a shorter version.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 12, 'Set your phone to do not disturb for one hour and tell the people who might need to know.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 13, 'Write down one boundary you wish you had held recently and how you would say it next time.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 14, 'Ask for what you need today in one clear sentence: "I need some quiet for an hour."'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 15, 'Let someone else handle something you would normally take over.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 16, 'Say "That does not work for me" once today and leave it there.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 17, 'Take your full break at work or school today, away from your desk if you can.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 18, 'Notice a guilty feeling after saying no and remind yourself: guilt is not proof you did something wrong.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 19, 'Decide on one topic you will not discuss with a particular person, and change the subject if it comes up.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 20, 'Write down the difference between what someone wants from you and what you owe them.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 21, 'Give yourself an hour today that no one else gets to schedule.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 22, 'Practice a gentle exit line: "I need to go now, let''s talk soon."'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 23, 'Notice one person who respects your boundaries easily and thank them for it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 24, 'Say "I will think about it" to something you are tempted to agree to on the spot.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 25, 'Stop doing one thing today that you only do to avoid someone''s disappointment.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 26, 'Tell someone how you would like to be spoken to, calmly, in one sentence.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 27, 'Set a limit on one thing that drains you, screen time, a group chat, and hold it today.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 28, 'Write down what you are afraid will happen if you hold a boundary. Then write what usually actually happens.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 29, 'Hold one boundary today and afterward write down how your body felt.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 30, 'Reread your notes from this challenge and pick the one boundary that matters most. Write it as a sentence you can say.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 31, 'Before you answer any request this morning, take one full breath and ask yourself whether you actually have the time.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 32, 'Write down the three people you find it hardest to say no to. Next to each name, note why.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 33, 'Practice saying "I would rather not" in the mirror until it sounds ordinary rather than dramatic.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 34, 'Decline one meeting invitation today that has no clear reason for you to be there.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 35, 'Notice one request today that arrived as a statement rather than a question, and answer it as if it were a question.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 36, 'End a phone call at the time you said you would, even if the other person is still talking.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 37, 'Say "I can do half of that" to one task today instead of taking all of it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 38, 'Pick one chore at home that is not yours and leave it undone for someone else to do.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 39, 'Tell a friend one thing you would like to change about how your time together usually goes.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 40, 'Write down a boundary you hold easily with strangers and ask why it is harder with people you love.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 41, 'Choose a cutoff time for reading work email tonight and close the app at that time.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 42, 'Ask a coworker to send their request in writing so you can consider it before you respond.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 43, 'Say "I do not lend that" or "I do not share that" about one possession today, kindly and without a story.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 44, 'Notice when you nod along in a conversation today and see if you can stay still instead.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 45, 'Mute one group chat for the rest of the day and see what changes.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 46, 'Tell one person what time you need to leave before an event begins, so leaving is not a surprise.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 47, 'Write down what a "soft no" sounds like for you and what a "clear no" sounds like. Use the clear one once.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 48, 'Let a phone call from a family member go to voicemail and call back when you are ready.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 49, 'Refuse one favor today that you would have said yes to a month ago.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 50, 'Say "I am going to pass" to one invitation and resist the urge to add a reason.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 51, 'Ask yourself before bed: what did I give away today that I did not want to give?'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 52, 'Decide how many minutes you will spend on one draining errand and stop when the minutes are up.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 53, 'Tell your partner or housemate one thing you need them to stop doing in shared space.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 54, 'Practice the sentence "That is not something I can take on right now" until it fits in your mouth.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 55, 'Turn off notifications for one app that pulls at you and leave them off through dinner.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 56, 'Say what you want to eat when someone asks, rather than "whatever you like."'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 57, 'Write down one way you make yourself smaller to keep someone comfortable, and skip it once today.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 58, 'Ask for the deadline before you agree to a task at work, then decide whether it is realistic.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 59, 'Sit down to eat lunch today without answering messages, and tell anyone waiting that you will reply afterward.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 60, 'Give a short, honest answer when someone asks how you are, instead of the automatic "fine."'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 61, 'Notice a request today that came with flattery attached and separate the compliment from the ask.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 62, 'Close your laptop at the end of the workday and put it somewhere out of sight.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 63, 'Say "Please ask me first next time" to someone who assumed you would be available.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 64, 'Write a two-sentence reply to a long message instead of matching its length.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 65, 'Tell a friend you need to reschedule because you are tired, without dressing up the reason.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 66, 'Choose one thing you will not volunteer for this month and write it down.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 67, 'Notice one person who tends to talk over you and finish your sentence anyway.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 68, 'Say "I need to think about whether I have room for that" to one request and mean it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 69, 'Set a limit on how late you will stay at a social event tonight and leave then.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 70, 'Write down three things you are responsible for and three things that are not yours to carry.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 71, 'Ask a family member to knock before entering your room, and say why it matters to you.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 72, 'Turn down an extra shift or extra project today if you were already at capacity.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 73, 'Practice saying "No thank you" without lowering your voice or looking away.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 74, 'Notice how you feel in the first minute after saying no and write one word for it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 75, 'Tell someone who keeps rescheduling on you what you need from them going forward.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 76, 'Decline to explain a decision when someone pushes for reasons you do not owe them.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 77, 'Set a rule about what hours you will answer texts from a particular person and follow it tonight.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 78, 'Say "I am not the right person for that" to one request that lands on you by habit.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 79, 'Write down one thing you are tired of being the default for, and name who else could do it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 80, 'Ask a colleague to take a turn with a task you usually handle, and let them do it their way.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 81, 'Say "I will let you know by Friday" instead of answering a big ask on the spot.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 82, 'Notice a moment today when you laughed at something that bothered you, and say what you felt instead.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 83, 'Put your phone in another room for the first hour of the morning.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 84, 'Tell someone who asks for advice that you would rather just listen today.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 85, 'Write down the last time you said yes out of fear of seeming rude. What would you say now?'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 86, 'Leave a conversation that has turned into complaining by saying you need a break.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 87, 'Pick one social obligation on your calendar you dread and decide honestly whether to keep it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 88, 'Say "That is your decision to make" when someone tries to hand you a choice that belongs to them.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 89, 'Ask to be removed from one email thread or mailing list that adds nothing to your day.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 90, 'Practice a gentle interruption today: "I want to add something before we move on."'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 91, 'Tell a friend or relative that you will not be answering messages during your vacation.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 92, 'Write down one thing you keep doing for someone that they could do themselves.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 93, 'Notice the pull to fix a problem someone mentioned today, and let it stay theirs.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 94, 'Say "I need a minute" and take it, instead of answering while overwhelmed.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 95, 'Tell someone the truth about why you did not come, rather than a polite excuse.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 96, 'Ask a neighbor or coworker to give you a heads-up before dropping by.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 97, 'Decide how much of your weekend belongs to you and block it off before anyone else claims it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 98, 'Write the boundary you find hardest to say as a text message, then decide whether to send it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 99, 'Turn down a request from someone you admire, and notice that admiration does not require a yes.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 100, 'Say "I am at capacity" to one person today, and let the phrase stand on its own.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 101, 'Start the morning by writing one sentence about what you will protect today: an hour, a task, a mood.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 102, 'Tell a coworker who messages after hours that you will see it in the morning, then do not open it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 103, 'Practice saying "I hear you, and my answer is still no" in a calm voice.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 104, 'Notice one moment today when you said "sorry" for taking up space and replace it with "thank you for waiting."'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 105, 'Ask someone who borrowed something to return it by a specific day.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 106, 'Decline a plan this weekend if you were only going to avoid letting someone down.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 107, 'Write down what you would do with an extra free evening this week, then clear one.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 108, 'Say "I would like to finish my thought" the next time you are cut off.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 109, 'Set a specific end time for helping a friend with a task, and tell them when you start.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 110, 'Tell your family which holiday traditions you will join this year and which you will skip.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 111, 'Notice one favor you are about to offer before anyone asks, and hold it back to see if it is needed.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 112, 'Write a script for declining an invitation from someone who takes no personally, and keep it in your phone.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 113, 'Refuse to be put on speakerphone or added to a call you did not agree to join.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 114, 'Pick one recurring commitment and ask yourself whether you would sign up for it again today.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 115, 'Tell a friend who vents at length that you have twenty minutes and then need to go.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 116, 'Say "I am choosing not to" instead of "I can''t" once today and notice the difference.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 117, 'Turn off your camera or leave a video call when your part is done.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 118, 'Write down what someone''s silence after your no is telling you, and what it is not telling you.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 119, 'Let a dish, a text, or a small errand wait until you have eaten.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 120, 'Ask your partner or a close friend what boundary of yours they notice you not holding.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 121, 'Say no to a second helping, a second drink, or a second round when you have had enough, and leave it at that.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 122, 'Decide what you will and will not talk about at a family meal, and stick with it.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 123, 'Notice a moment when someone changes the subject away from what you asked for. Ask again.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 124, 'Tell a relative that you will not be discussing your relationship, your job, or your plans tonight.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 125, 'Write a boundary for your workspace at home: hours, noise, interruptions, and share it with anyone it affects.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 126, 'Say "I am not comfortable with that" about one thing today, without softening it afterward.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 127, 'Take the last slice, the good seat, or the first turn once today without checking that it is okay.'),
  ('holding-your-boundaries', 128, 'Decline to answer a personal question from a coworker by saying "I keep that private."'),
