  ('meeting-anger-early', 1, 'Write down the last three things that made you angry. Look for what they have in common.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 2, 'Notice where anger shows up in your body first today: jaw, chest, hands, stomach.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 3, 'When you feel a flash of anger, breathe out slowly for a count of six before you say anything.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 4, 'Practice the phrase "I need a minute" and use it once today if you need it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 5, 'Write down what you were really feeling underneath your last angry moment. Hurt? Scared? Tired?'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 6, 'Unclench your hands and jaw on purpose five times today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 7, 'Take a ten-minute walk when something irritates you, before responding.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 8, 'Say "I feel frustrated when..." instead of "You always..." once today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 9, 'Rate your anger from zero to ten when you notice it. Respond only when it is under five.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 10, 'Splash cold water on your face or hold something cold when your temper rises.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 11, 'Write down what you would want to say in the heat of the moment. Then wait an hour and reread it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 12, 'Notice one small annoyance today and let it go without commenting.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 13, 'Ask yourself, "What do I need right now?" when you feel angry, and try to give it to yourself.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 14, 'Move your body hard for two minutes, stairs, a fast walk, when anger builds.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 15, 'Get enough to eat and drink today. Hunger and thirst make everything sharper.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 16, 'Write a list of your early warning signs of anger and keep it on your phone.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 17, 'Delay one reaction by ten minutes today and see if the same response still feels right.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 18, 'Say sorry for something small today, cleanly, without explaining why you did it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 19, 'Notice one thought that fuels your anger, like "they did that on purpose," and write down another possibility.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 20, 'Tell someone calmly what you would like them to do differently, in one sentence.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 21, 'Take three slow breaths before you open a message or email that might annoy you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 22, 'Spend ten minutes doing something physical and productive, cleaning, chopping, digging, when tension builds.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 23, 'Write down what anger has cost you recently and what it has protected.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 24, 'Practice lowering your voice on purpose in one tense moment today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 25, 'Ask a question instead of making an accusation once today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 26, 'Leave a conversation that is getting heated and come back to it later, saying that you will.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 27, 'Notice what you are tired of today and say it in plain words to someone who can help.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 28, 'Do something soothing for your body tonight: a stretch, a warm shower, an early night.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 29, 'Write down one thing you handled well today when you could have gotten angry.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 30, 'Review your notes from this challenge and pick the one early sign of anger you can now spot. Watch for it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 31, 'Before you get in the car today, decide what you will do when another driver cuts you off: one slow breath, then let them have the lane.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 32, 'Notice the moment your voice starts to speed up today. Slow your next sentence down on purpose.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 33, 'Put your phone face down for five minutes when a message makes your chest tighten, and pick it up only once your shoulders have dropped.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 34, 'When a family member says something that stings, name the feeling silently, "that hurt," before you answer.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 35, 'Count the number of times you sigh sharply today. Each one is an early signal worth noticing.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 36, 'Drink a full glass of water the next time you feel your temper rise, slowly, and see what has changed by the last sip.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 37, 'When a customer service call gets frustrating, write the one thing you actually want on a sticky note and keep your eyes on it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 38, 'Notice if you are holding your breath when you read the news today. Let it out and unclench your stomach.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 39, 'Pick one recurring argument with your partner and write down what you both seem to want underneath it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 40, 'When your kids ignore a request, lower yourself to their eye level and repeat it once, quietly, before doing anything else.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 41, 'Try saying "Help me understand" instead of "Why would you do that" once today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 42, 'Step outside for sixty seconds of fresh air the next time a work message makes you bristle.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 43, 'Write down the story you tell yourself when a friend is late. Then write the most boring explanation instead.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 44, 'Notice how anger changes your walking pace today. Slow your steps deliberately for one block.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 45, 'When you feel the urge to interrupt, press your tongue to the roof of your mouth and let the other person finish.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 46, 'Draft a reply to an irritating email, then delete the first sentence before you send it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 47, 'Name your anger a number out loud, quietly, to yourself, the next time it appears: "That is a four."'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 48, 'Notice one small kindness someone shows you today, right after a moment that annoyed you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 49, 'Warm your hands around a hot drink when tension builds and let the warmth do some of the work.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 50, 'When a roommate leaves a mess, decide whether to mention it now, later, or never, before saying a word.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 51, 'Ask yourself "Will this matter in a week?" before responding to one irritation today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 52, 'Put both feet flat on the floor and feel the ground when you notice heat rising in your face.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 53, 'Practice the sentence "I want to get this right, so give me a moment" and use it in one conversation today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 54, 'Set a timer for two minutes and do nothing but breathe when a disagreement starts to escalate.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 55, 'Notice what time of day you are most irritable. Plan one small comfort for that hour tomorrow.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 56, 'Say "You might be right" to someone today, even if only about a small point.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 57, 'When a driver honks at you, hum a few notes of a song you like before you react.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 58, 'Write down three things that usually happen right before you lose your temper. Watch for the first one tomorrow.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 59, 'Stretch your neck slowly from side to side the next time you notice tension building there.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 60, 'Tell a coworker what you need from them in the form of a request, not a complaint, once today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 61, 'Notice when you start rehearsing an argument in your head. Gently switch to naming five objects in the room.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 62, 'Before replying to a group chat that annoys you, read the message again as if a friend had sent it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 63, 'When your partner forgets something, say what you noticed without adding "again."'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 64, 'Loosen your grip on the steering wheel, your phone, or your pen when you catch yourself squeezing.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 65, 'Pause for the length of one full breath after someone finishes speaking before you answer them today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 66, 'Ask a child in your life what they think happened before you decide who is at fault.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 67, 'Write down what a calm version of you would say in the situation that bothered you most today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 68, 'Notice if your eyebrows are pulled together right now. Let your forehead go smooth.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 69, 'Give one person the benefit of the doubt today and see if the irritation fades on its own.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 70, 'When a website or app fails on you, stand up and stretch before you try again.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 71, 'Speak your next frustrated sentence at half the volume you feel like using.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 72, 'Say "Let me think about that" instead of answering right away in one tense moment today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 73, 'Notice which people leave you feeling short-tempered. Plan a little extra rest before seeing one of them.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 74, 'Put an ice cube in your palm and hold it until it starts to sting the next time your temper spikes.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 75, 'Write down the last time someone was angry at you and what would have helped you hear them.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 76, 'Ask yourself "Am I tired?" the next time a small thing feels enormous.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 77, 'When waiting in a slow line, count the ceiling tiles or floor squares instead of the minutes.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 78, 'Roll your shoulders back and down three times when you feel yourself hunching in irritation.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 79, 'Tell someone "I am not upset with you, I am upset about the situation" when it is true today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 80, 'Notice the first word that comes to mind when you get angry today. Write it down without judging it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 81, 'Wait until your heartbeat feels steady before sending any reply you wrote while annoyed.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 82, 'Pick a calm object in your home, a plant, a photo, a mug, and look at it for ten seconds when you feel yourself heating up.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 83, 'When a meeting runs long and you feel restless, plant your feet and relax your hands under the table.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 84, 'Practice saying "That is frustrating" out loud to yourself instead of swallowing it or shouting it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 85, 'Write one sentence about what you are afraid will happen if you do not get angry.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 86, 'Notice if you are skipping meals today and eat something before any difficult conversation.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 87, 'Turn your phone to silent for an hour when the notifications are keeping you on edge.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 88, 'When someone cuts in front of you in a line, take a slow breath and decide if it is worth a word. Either choice is fine.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 89, 'Rub your palms together slowly for ten seconds and feel the warmth when you notice your hands tensing.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 90, 'Ask your partner "What would help right now?" instead of guessing during one tense moment.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 91, 'Notice a rising tone in your own voice and finish the sentence more softly than you started it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 92, 'Plan one thing to say when your child pushes a boundary tonight, and say only that.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 93, 'Reread an angry text you almost sent and underline every word that is about the past, not the present.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 94, 'Let one small mistake by someone else pass without correcting it today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 95, 'Notice when you clench your teeth while driving and let your jaw hang loose at the next red light.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 96, 'Say "I need to pause this" and take a short walk when an argument with a family member loops.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 97, 'Write down what you want the other person to understand, in ten words or fewer, before you speak.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 98, 'Listen to a slow piece of music for three minutes when you feel yourself winding up.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 99, 'When a coworker takes credit for your work, wait until tomorrow to raise it, and note how you feel then.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 100, 'Notice whether your breathing is high in your chest right now. Move it lower with one long exhale.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 101, 'Sit down before you respond to something that made you angry today. Standing tends to keep the heat up.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 102, 'Ask yourself "What else could be true?" about one situation that irritated you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 103, 'Describe an annoying event to yourself in the plainest words possible, no adjectives, and see how it feels.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 104, 'Wash your hands slowly with warm water when you notice tension in your fingers.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 105, 'Tell someone a small thing that is bothering you before it becomes a big thing.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 106, 'Write down one habit of yours that other people probably find irritating. Let it soften your view of theirs.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 107, 'When traffic stops, look at something far away, a tree, a sign, the sky, and let your eyes rest there.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 108, 'Notice the urge to slam a door or drawer today. Close it slowly instead and feel the difference.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 109, 'Practice one apology in the mirror for something you said sharply, then deliver it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 110, 'Give yourself thirty seconds of silence before answering a question that feels like an accusation.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 111, 'Say what you see, "the dishes are still in the sink," without saying what it means about the person.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 112, 'Notice if you are replaying the same irritation from yesterday. Give it a name and set it aside for tonight.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 113, 'Place a hand on your chest for three breaths when you feel your heart pounding with anger.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 114, 'Ask a coworker to repeat what they said before you react, and listen the second time for what they meant.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 115, 'Choose one small task to do with full attention when you feel restless anger, folding laundry, washing a cup.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 116, 'When your kids are loud and you feel the snap coming, step into another room for one minute first.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 117, 'Write a short list of what you can control in a situation that angers you. Act on only that.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 118, 'Notice your posture during one disagreement today and let your shoulders drop while you listen.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 119, 'Tell your partner one thing they did today that you appreciated, especially if you have been irritated with them.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 120, 'Take the stairs slowly instead of quickly when you feel worked up, and count each step.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 121, 'Pick a word that means "pause" to you and say it silently the next time your temper rises.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 122, 'Before a difficult conversation, decide what a good ending would look like and keep it in mind.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 123, 'Let a rude comment online go unanswered today. Notice how quickly it loses its weight.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 124, 'Loosen your belt, tie, or collar when you feel yourself heating up. A little physical ease helps.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 125, 'Ask yourself "Is this about now or about something older?" when a small thing feels too big.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 126, 'Write down the kindest interpretation of something that annoyed you today, even if you do not believe it yet.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 127, 'Notice when a "should" runs through your head, "they should know better," and try "I wish" instead.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 128, 'Look at the person you are angry with and notice one thing about them that is not about the argument.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 129, 'Stand at a window and watch something move, clouds, leaves, cars, for one minute when your chest is tight.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 130, 'When someone interrupts you, wait, then say "I was not finished" in a level voice.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 131, 'Try eating a piece of fruit slowly when irritation strikes, and let the task of eating settle you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 132, 'Notice the second thing that makes you angry today, and ask whether the first one is still burning.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 133, 'Say "I hear you" before you say anything else in one disagreement today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 134, 'Write down what you would tell a friend who was angry about the thing that angered you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 135, 'When a package is late or an order is wrong, start your complaint with what you would like to happen.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 136, 'Press your feet into the floor for five seconds when you feel the urge to storm off.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 137, 'Ask yourself whether you are hungry, hot, or tired before deciding someone did something wrong.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 138, 'Practice a neutral face in the mirror for ten seconds, then use it when a comment stings today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 139, 'Give a roommate or partner a specific time you would like to talk instead of raising it in passing.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 140, 'Notice how quickly you form a judgment about a stranger who annoys you. Wait five seconds before deciding anything.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 141, 'Breathe in for four counts and out for eight when you feel your fists start to close.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 142, 'Tell yourself "This is anger arriving" the moment you notice the first sign today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 143, 'Write down one thing you say when angry that you would never say when calm. Retire that phrase.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 144, 'Put down whatever you are holding before you respond to something that makes you angry.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 145, 'Let the phone ring one extra time before answering a call you expect to be difficult.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 146, 'Notice when you start speaking in absolutes, "never," "always," "every time," and swap one for a specific example.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 147, 'Take a sip of something before every sentence in one tense conversation today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 148, 'Ask your child to tell you the story from the beginning before you react to the ending.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 149, 'Look for one sign of stress in the person who annoyed you today. It may explain more than you think.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 150, 'Give yourself permission to say "I do not know yet" instead of defending a position in the heat of the moment.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 151, 'When a driver tailgates you, move over if you can and let them go. Say "not my race" quietly.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 152, 'Write down the physical sensation of anger fading. Notice that it does fade, every time.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 153, 'Notice if you are scrolling faster when something online riles you. Put the device down for a minute.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 154, 'Say "That is not what I meant" calmly when misunderstood, instead of repeating yourself louder.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 155, 'Trace the outline of your hand slowly with a finger, one breath per finger, when you need to cool down.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 156, 'Ask what a coworker is dealing with today before assuming their tone was about you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 157, 'Notice the difference between being angry and being right. Choose which one you want more in one moment today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 158, 'Tell someone what you are angry about in one sentence, then stop talking and let them respond.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 159, 'Take a different route home tonight if the usual one tends to leave you frustrated.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 160, 'Practice unclenching your stomach muscles when you notice they are tight during a conversation.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 161, 'Write down what you needed from a parent when you were little and angry. See if you can offer that to yourself today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 162, 'Pause a video game or show when you notice frustration building instead of pushing through it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 163, 'Say "I might be misreading this" before you accuse someone of anything today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 164, 'Notice your first thought when a plan falls through. Write down a second, calmer one beside it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 165, 'Hold a warm mug and do nothing else for two minutes after a hard phone call.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 166, 'Leave a review or complaint until tomorrow if you are writing it angry tonight.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 167, 'Ask a partner or friend to tell you what they notice when your temper starts to rise. Listen without defending.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 168, 'When an appliance or car fails, say out loud "This is inconvenient, not a disaster" before you do anything.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 169, 'Practice walking away from a screen mid-argument online, and do not come back to it for an hour.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 170, 'Notice if you are keeping score in a relationship today. Set the tally down for one evening.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 171, 'Tell your kids "I am feeling frustrated and I am taking a breath" so they can see what it looks like.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 172, 'Wait for the other person to take a breath before you speak in one tense exchange today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 173, 'Pick one thing you are angry about and ask what a fair outcome would be, not a winning one.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 174, 'Hum, quietly, for thirty seconds when you notice your throat tightening with anger.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 175, 'Write the name of the person you are angry with, then three things they do well.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 176, 'Notice when you want to be understood more than you want to solve the problem. Say so.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 177, 'Give yourself a small task with your hands, sorting, wiping, tying, before you answer a heated message.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 178, 'Ask "What would make this easier for both of us?" during one disagreement today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 179, 'Say nothing for a full minute when someone criticizes you, then respond to only the fair part.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 180, 'Notice the temperature of your face when anger arrives. Cool it with a wet cloth if you can.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 181, 'Set your phone to do-not-disturb during dinner if the interruptions tend to make you snap.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 182, 'Look up from your screen and name the colors you can see when you feel yourself getting worked up.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 183, 'When a neighbor is noisy, write down your request before knocking, and keep it to two sentences.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 184, 'Practice saying "I am upset" in a flat voice, so the words carry the message instead of the volume.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 185, 'Notice whether you are standing too close to someone during a disagreement, and take one step back.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 186, 'Ask yourself "What am I protecting?" when anger flares. Often it is something you care about.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 187, 'Turn a tight fist into an open hand slowly, finger by finger, when you catch it clenched.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 188, 'Write down one boundary you keep forgetting to state, and say it today, plainly and early.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 189, 'Let a slow driver in front of you set your pace for one mile without changing lanes.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 190, 'Notice when you are speaking for someone else, "you think I am stupid," and ask them instead.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 191, 'Try a cold drink of water before you respond to a message that made your jaw tighten.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 192, 'Say "Give me a second to calm down" to a family member and take that second.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 193, 'Pick one comment from today that annoyed you and ask whether the person knew it would.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 194, 'Notice when your anger is really about not being heard, and ask for two minutes of full attention.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 195, 'Breathe out longer than you breathe in for five rounds when tension climbs in your shoulders.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 196, 'Write down the thing you keep not saying to a partner or roommate, then say the gentlest version of it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 197, 'Sit with your back supported and feet on the floor before a phone call you expect to be hard.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 198, 'Ask your coworker for their reasons before you share your objections in one meeting today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 199, 'Notice if you are gripping your jaw while you sleep or wake. Yawn wide a few times in the morning.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 200, 'Give a rude stranger an imaginary bad day in your head, then let them go.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 201, 'When customer service puts you on hold, use the time to relax your hands and slow your breath.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 202, 'Say "I want to solve this with you, not against you" once in a disagreement today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 203, 'Notice which topics make you defensive fastest. Write one down and plan a slower response.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 204, 'Take one deep breath in through your nose and feel your ribs expand before answering anything sharp.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 205, 'Tell someone "I am going to think about that" and actually come back with a thought later.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 206, 'Write a message you will never send to someone who made you angry, then close the file.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 207, 'Notice the urge to have the last word today, and let someone else have it once.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 208, 'Feel the weight of your body in the chair for three breaths when a meeting frustrates you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 209, 'Ask your partner to describe the problem from their side before you describe it from yours.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 210, 'Change rooms, or step into the hall, when a conversation with a family member starts to sharpen.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 211, 'Practice one soft opening line, "Can I check something with you?" and use it instead of a complaint.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 212, 'Notice if a screen is making you angrier than the situation is. Turn it off for ten minutes.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 213, 'When someone is wrong about a small fact, let them be wrong today and notice what it costs you. Probably nothing.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 214, 'Look at a photo of someone you love when you feel a surge of anger at work.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 215, 'Say "I am starting to feel heated" the moment you notice it, to yourself or to the person in front of you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 216, 'Give your body five slow shoulder shrugs when you feel the tension of an unresolved argument.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 217, 'Write down what you assume about someone''s intentions, then ask them one question to check it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 218, 'Notice when you are matching someone else''s volume. Drop yours by a notch and see if they follow.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 219, 'Take your hands off the keyboard for one minute when a work message makes you want to fire back.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 220, 'Ask a child what they need instead of what they did, in one moment of frustration today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 221, 'Stand up and shake out your arms and hands when you feel stuck in a loop of irritation.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 222, 'Tell a friend about something that angered you and ask them what they see in it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 223, 'Wait until you can say a sentence without a sharp edge before you say anything at all.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 224, 'Notice one thing that usually makes you angry and does not today. Ask yourself what was different.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 225, 'Breathe in the smell of something you like, coffee, soap, fresh air, when you feel a flash of anger.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 226, 'Describe your anger as weather to yourself today: a squall, a heat wave, a passing cloud.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 227, 'Let your partner finish their whole point before you respond, even if you disagree from the first word.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 228, 'Say "I was wrong about that" once today, and notice that nothing bad happens.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 229, 'Choose the slowest checkout line on purpose and practice being fine with it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 230, 'Notice the moment right before you raise your voice. That moment is where the choice lives.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 231, 'Ask yourself "What would I want them to do if I had made this mistake?" before you correct someone.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 232, 'Write down what you do well when you are angry, staying honest, standing up for someone, and keep that part.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 233, 'Put a hand on a wall or table and feel how solid it is when your anger feels unsteady.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 234, 'Practice a two-second delay before every reply in one conversation with your kids today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 235, 'When a coworker misses a deadline, ask what got in the way before you say what it cost you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 236, 'Notice if you are angry at a person or at a system. Aim your energy at the right one.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 237, 'Give the person you are annoyed with a full sentence of your attention before deciding how to answer.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 238, 'Tell yourself "I can be angry and still be kind" the next time both feel impossible.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 239, 'Set down your bag, keys, or coat and take one breath before you speak when you come home tense.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 240, 'Ask for what you want by name instead of hinting once today, and notice whether the anger shrinks.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 241, 'Notice when you are angry because a plan changed. Say "I was looking forward to that" instead of blaming.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 242, 'Walk to the mailbox, the corner, or the end of the hall before you answer a message that stung.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 243, 'Write one sentence of appreciation to someone you have been short with this week.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 244, 'Say "That landed badly" instead of "You are being rude" when a comment hurts today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 245, 'Notice the cost of being right in one argument today. Decide if it is worth paying.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 246, 'Take a slow drink and swallow before responding when a family member pushes a familiar button.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 247, 'Try keeping your hands loose in your lap during a tense video call.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 248, 'Ask a roommate "Is now a good time?" before raising something that bothers you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 249, 'Look at the ceiling for five seconds and let your eyes soften when frustration flares.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 250, 'When someone forgets your name or your order, notice if it feels bigger than it is, and let it be small.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 251, 'Tell your partner about your early signs of anger so they can help you spot them.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 252, 'Notice when you are reading tone into a text message that may not be there. Ask instead of assuming.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 253, 'Breathe slowly through pursed lips, like cooling soup, when your temper heats up.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 254, 'Give yourself an evening away from the topic that has been making you angry all week.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 255, 'Say "I need this to change" in a calm voice, followed by exactly what needs to change.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 256, 'Write down what you notice in your hands, voice, and breath in the first thirty seconds of anger.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 257, 'Notice if you are angry about something you also do. Let that thought take a little air out of it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 258, 'Do a slow lap of your home or office before you decide how to respond to bad news.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 259, 'Practice one sentence that starts with "I" and ends with a request, and use it at work today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 260, 'Ask your child what a fair solution would be before you announce one.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 261, 'Let a car merge in front of you and wave, even if you do not feel like it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 262, 'Notice when you are tensing to defend yourself before anyone has attacked. Relax and wait to see what actually comes.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 263, 'Sit on the floor with your back against a wall for one minute when anger has you pacing.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 264, 'Tell someone what you are not angry about, so they know the size of the problem.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 265, 'Write down the moment today when you cooled off fastest. What helped?'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 266, 'Check your jaw, shoulders, and hands once every hour today and loosen whichever is tight.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 267, 'Ask "Did I understand you correctly?" and repeat what you heard before you argue with it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 268, 'Choose to read the whole email before reacting to the first line that annoyed you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 269, 'Notice the pull to prove a point online today. Close the tab instead.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 270, 'Take a longer route to the kitchen or bathroom when you need to cool down between tasks.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 271, 'Say "I am glad you told me" when someone criticizes you today, even if you have to say it twice to mean it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 272, 'Pause the conversation and offer to make tea or coffee when a family disagreement sharpens.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 273, 'Notice the story that begins with "they never" today. Find one time they did.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 274, 'Give a small, real compliment to the person who annoyed you most this morning.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 275, 'Write down how long your last angry moment lasted, from first sign to calm. Notice it was shorter than it felt.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 276, 'Lower your shoulders, then your voice, then your pace, in that order, when you feel the heat coming.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 277, 'Ask yourself "What is the smallest thing I could say here?" and say only that.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 278, 'Notice what your anger wants you to do, and do something one notch gentler.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 279, 'Set your phone across the room during a conversation that tends to get heated.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 280, 'Tell a coworker "I disagree, and I want to hear more" before you explain why.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 281, 'Breathe out with a quiet sigh on purpose, three times, when your patience runs thin.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 282, 'When the same driver, coworker, or relative gets on your nerves again, try saying "there it is" to yourself and nothing more.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 283, 'Practice sitting with the discomfort of not responding to something for a whole hour.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 284, 'Write down one thing you learned about your anger this week and one thing you still want to know.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 285, 'Notice if you are thirsty right now. Drink before you do anything about what is bothering you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 286, 'Look at your hands while someone speaks to you in a tense moment, and keep them open.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 287, 'Give a kid a choice between two acceptable options instead of a command when you feel your patience thinning.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 288, 'Ask your partner to hold your hand for ten seconds before you talk about something difficult.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 289, 'Say "I am going to be honest and I am going to be calm" to yourself before a hard conversation.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 290, 'Notice if your anger came with a wave of shame. Treat the shame gently and the anger will often follow.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 291, 'Pause and name three things you are grateful for about a person you are frustrated with.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 292, 'Let the moment pass without commentary when someone else is rude to a stranger in front of you, unless someone needs help.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 293, 'Write down what you would lose if you stayed angry all evening. Then choose something else to do.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 294, 'Try a slow yawn on purpose when you feel your face tighten. It loosens more than the jaw.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 295, 'Notice the point at which a conversation stops being useful, and suggest a break at that point instead of after.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 296, 'Ask someone at work to give you the short version before you react to a long, frustrating message.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 297, 'Remind yourself that a raised voice rarely changes a mind, then lower yours.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 298, 'Take a moment at the door before entering a room where you expect friction, and set your face and shoulders.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 299, 'Speak to the person, not the audience, when a disagreement happens in front of others today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 300, 'Notice a small irritation you have been carrying since morning and set it down before lunch.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 301, 'Give yourself credit for every moment today that you noticed anger before it spoke.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 302, 'Write down one thing you could say that would make the situation worse. Then do not say it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 303, 'Practice making eye contact and breathing slowly, at the same time, during one tense exchange.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 304, 'When your order is wrong at a restaurant, say what you would like fixed in one friendly sentence.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 305, 'Tell yourself "This is a sign, not a verdict" when your body flares with anger today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 306, 'Ask a friend to point out when your tone gets sharp, and thank them when they do.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 307, 'Notice if you have been carrying yesterday''s argument in your shoulders. Let them drop.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 308, 'Pick the calmest word you know for how you feel and use it instead of the sharpest.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 309, 'Give a difficult person a full day off from your thoughts. Notice when they creep back, and let them go again.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 310, 'Say what you want to happen next, in plain words, to the person who upset you today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 311, 'Sit outside for five minutes before going back into a house or office where you felt tense.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 312, 'Notice what you are clenching right now, then release it slowly and wait for the next sign.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 313, 'Turn your body slightly away from a screen or person when you feel your anger rising, and breathe.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 314, 'Write down what you will do the next time your usual early sign shows up, in one line, and keep it where you can see it.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 315, 'Notice how you talk to yourself after you lose your temper. Try one sentence that a patient friend would use.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 316, 'Ask the person who annoyed you what they were hoping for. Their answer may surprise you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 317, 'When a coworker replies to all with something that irritates you, respond to one person, tomorrow, or not at all.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 318, 'Try describing what happened to a pet, a plant, or an empty room before you describe it to the person involved.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 319, 'Tell your teenager "I am too angry to talk well right now, give me twenty minutes" and then come back in twenty.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 320, 'Let a slow elevator, printer, or website be slow today without narrating your frustration out loud.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 321, 'Write one line about what anger feels like in your feet and legs. Most people never check there.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 322, 'Rinse a dish or wipe a counter slowly when you need a minute to cool before answering someone.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 323, 'Notice when your partner''s tone reminds you of someone from the past. Answer the person in front of you.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 324, 'Practice saying "I am frustrated with the plan, not with you" to a family member when it is true.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 325, 'Give yourself a full breath in and out before you touch the horn.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 326, 'Say "Ouch" quietly when a comment stings, and let that be your whole reaction for a moment.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 327, 'Find one thing in the room that is the color blue and study it when heat rises in your chest.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 328, 'Ask yourself "Would I say this if they could hear me?" before you mutter about someone today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 329, 'Speak to a customer service agent as if they wrote none of the policy that is annoying you, because they did not.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 330, 'Notice when a joke at your expense turns your stomach. Say "I did not love that" in a level voice.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 331, 'Move to a cooler room, open a window, or step into shade when your temper and the temperature rise together.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 332, 'Plan a small, specific reward for yourself after a conversation you expect to be tense.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 333, 'Let a text from a family member sit unanswered for twenty minutes if the first read made you clench.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 334, 'Write down the one thing you most want your roommate to know, then say it without the word "always."'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 335, 'Notice if you are angry on someone else''s behalf today. Ask them what they want before you act.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 336, 'Take a slow breath before pressing "send," "post," or "reply" on anything you wrote while heated.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 337, 'Try answering a sharp question with a soft question in return, "What makes you ask?"'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 338, 'Watch a child, a bird, or a dog for one minute when you feel anger looping in your mind.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 339, 'Keep your voice at a normal speaking level during one disagreement, no matter what the other person does with theirs.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 340, 'Ask yourself what you would need to hear to calm down, and offer that sentence to the other person first.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 341, 'Tell your body "we are safe" in plain words when it braces for a fight over something small.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 342, 'Practice saying no to one request today without sharpness and without over-explaining.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 343, 'Notice if you are angry because you said yes to too much. Take one thing off your plate.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 344, 'Stir, pour, or chop something slowly for two minutes when a family evening starts to fray.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 345, 'Put a note on your fridge that says "Notice first" and read it every time you pass it today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 346, 'When a parent or in-law criticizes your choices, breathe, then say "I hear that you are worried."'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 347, 'Write down which of your early signs of anger you saw first today, and which one came second.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 348, 'Give your feet a slow stretch, toes up and down, when frustration shows up during a long sit.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 349, 'Try "I would prefer" in place of "You should" in one exchange with a partner or coworker today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 350, 'Look for a small way to make a task easier for the person who is annoying you, and do it quietly.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 351, 'Notice when your anger is masking disappointment. Name the disappointment to yourself first.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 352, 'Set a rule for yourself today: no important conversations after ten at night.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 353, 'Ask your child to help you solve the problem instead of telling them the solution.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 354, 'Try counting backward from twenty, slowly, when a stranger''s behavior makes your blood rise.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 355, 'Read back your last three messages in a heated thread and notice which one turned the temperature up.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 356, 'Say "I care about this, that is why I am upset" so the other person knows what the heat is about.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 357, 'Loosen your gaze and take in the whole room, not just the face in front of you, during a tense moment.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 358, 'Wait until tomorrow to decide whether the thing that angered you today deserves a response.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 359, 'Notice the softest moment in an argument you had this week. See if you can start there next time.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 360, 'Practice standing still with your hands at your sides for thirty seconds when you want to pace or storm off.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 361, 'Give someone a chance to correct themselves before you correct them, with a simple "Do you mean...?"'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 362, 'Tell yourself the truth about how much sleep you got last night before you judge how anyone treated you today.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 363, 'Ask what a friend would notice about your body language right now, and adjust one thing.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 364, 'Say the name of the person you are talking to, gently, before you say something hard to hear.'),
  ('meeting-anger-early', 365, 'Rest your hands palm-up on your knees for one minute after a frustrating call, and let them stay open.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 1, 'Write down three things you have done in your life that were hard at the time and that you managed.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 2, 'Speak first in one conversation today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 3, 'Stand up straight, shoulders back, for one minute and notice how it changes your mood.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 4, 'Ask a question in a meeting, a class, or a shop today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 5, 'Write down one skill you are good at and one piece of evidence for it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 6, 'Wear something today that makes you feel like yourself.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 7, 'Say your opinion once today without adding "but I might be wrong."'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 8, 'Make one small decision quickly today and do not revisit it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 9, 'Introduce yourself to someone new.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 10, 'Set a tiny goal for today and finish it. Write "done" next to it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 11, 'Accept a compliment with only "thank you."'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 12, 'Try something you are not good at yet for ten minutes, just to practice being a beginner.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 13, 'Write down what a confident version of you would do today. Do one part of it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 14, 'Make a phone call you have been avoiding.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 15, 'Look someone in the eye when you say hello today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 16, 'Write down one thing you did well this week that nobody noticed.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 17, 'Volunteer for one small thing, a task, an errand, a turn, before you have time to talk yourself out of it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 18, 'Practice saying "I don''t know, but I can find out."'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 19, 'Do one thing today that scares you a little, on a scale of one to ten a three or a four.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 20, 'Write down the worst-case outcome of something you are avoiding, then how you would handle it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 21, 'Notice one time today you compared yourself to someone and turn your attention back to your own next step.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 22, 'Ask for help with something today. Confident people do.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 23, 'Teach someone something small that you know.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 24, 'Sit at the front, or in the middle, instead of the back.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 25, 'Write down one thing you believe about yourself that is out of date.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 26, 'Speak a little slower and a little louder than usual in one conversation today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 27, 'Say no to something you do not want to do, once, and let it stand.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 28, 'List three people who believe in you and one thing each of them would say to you today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 29, 'Do something you are already good at and let yourself enjoy being good at it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 30, 'Read your list of small steps from this challenge and write down what you now know you can do.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 31, 'Order something at a cafe or restaurant without checking what anyone else is getting first.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 32, 'Send one email today without rereading it more than once before you hit send.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 33, 'Walk into a store, ask a staff member where something is, and thank them.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 34, 'Post a comment, review, or reply somewhere online under your own name.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 35, 'Give your honest answer when someone asks "what do you think?" instead of "I don''t mind."'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 36, 'Note one thing you did today that you would have avoided a month ago.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 37, 'Take the seat, the parking spot, or the spot in line that is yours without apologizing for it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 38, 'Ask a coworker or classmate to show you how they do one thing you have been guessing at.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 39, 'Try a new recipe, and if it goes wrong, eat it anyway and write down what you learned.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 40, 'Sign up for a class, a talk, a workshop, or a free online lesson you have been circling.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 41, 'Suggest a place, a time, or a plan when a group is going back and forth about what to do.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 42, 'Return an item to a store today, or ask about a refund, if you have been putting it off.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 43, 'Write down one compliment you received in the past year and the evidence that it was true.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 44, 'Tell someone about a small win today, out loud, without downplaying it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 45, 'Book the appointment you have been meaning to make, the dentist, the doctor, the haircut.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 46, 'Correct someone gently when they get your name, your role, or a fact about you wrong.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 47, 'Do the first five minutes of a task you feel unqualified for and see how far you get.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 48, 'Ask for a table, a room, or a seat with a better view when it is available.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 49, 'Share one idea in a group chat, a meeting, or a family conversation before anyone asks you.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 50, 'Learn one new word, phrase, or fact today and use it in conversation.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 51, 'Say "I would like" instead of "would it be okay if maybe" once today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 52, 'Send a message to someone you admire, a thank you, a question, or a hello.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 53, 'Wave, nod, or say good morning to a neighbor or a stranger on your street.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 54, 'Set a timer for fifteen minutes and work on the thing you keep saying you are not ready for.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 55, 'Ask a shop assistant for a recommendation and go with it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 56, 'Make one decision for a group today: where to eat, what to watch, when to leave.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 57, 'Write down one thing you know more about than most people you meet.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 58, 'Take a photo of something you made, fixed, or finished today and keep it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 59, 'Ask for feedback on one piece of your work and read it all the way through.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 60, 'Give a compliment to a stranger, the cashier, the bus driver, someone in line.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 61, 'Try a sport, a game, or an activity you have never played, for one round.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 62, 'Speak up in a small way when a plan does not work for you, and offer a different one.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 63, 'Sit somewhere new for lunch today, a different bench, room, or table.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 64, 'Call a business to ask a question instead of searching for the answer online.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 65, 'Write down what you would attempt this month if you knew it would go fine, then do the smallest piece.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 66, 'Wear the color or outfit you usually think is too much for you.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 67, 'Ask someone to teach you their favorite card game, board game, or phone game.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 68, 'Raise your hand or unmute first when a group is asked a question.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 69, 'Fix one small thing in your home today and stand back and look at it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 70, 'Hold a door, offer a seat, or help someone lift something, and accept their thanks.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 71, 'Send a short note to a former colleague or teacher and tell them what you are doing now.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 72, 'Practice a two-sentence answer to "what do you do?" and say it to someone today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 73, 'Go to an event, a class, or a gathering alone and stay for at least thirty minutes.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 74, 'Write down one mistake from this year and one thing you handled better because of it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 75, 'Ask a family member for their honest opinion on something you made and listen without arguing.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 76, 'Pick the harder of two small options today, the stairs, the longer walk, the new route.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 77, 'Leave a voicemail instead of hanging up when nobody answers.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 78, 'Say "I made that" or "I did that" when it is true, and stop there.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 79, 'Reply to a message you have been avoiding, even if the reply is short.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 80, 'Join a conversation that is already happening rather than waiting to be invited in.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 81, 'Try a haircut, a hat, or a style choice you have been talking yourself out of.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 82, 'Write down one thing you are proud of from this week and read it back out loud.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 83, 'Ask a clear question at the pharmacy, the bank, or the post office today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 84, 'Sing along, dance, or hum where someone else might hear you.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 85, 'Give yourself a small task with a deadline of noon, and meet it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 86, 'Tell someone what you need help with in one sentence, without an apology first.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 87, 'Take the lead on a small errand for your household and finish it start to end.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 88, 'Write a short list of things you can do now that you could not do two years ago.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 89, 'Ask a neighbor, coworker, or friend a question about their life and listen for the answer.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 90, 'Show someone a hobby project, a photo, a page, a drawing, before it is polished.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 91, 'Book yourself a slot in a public place, a library room, a gym class, a court, and show up.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 92, 'Pay for something and say "keep the change" or "no receipt, thanks" with a steady voice.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 93, 'Say hello to a coworker or classmate you have never talked to.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 94, 'Try answering one question in a quiz, a trivia night, or an online puzzle, even if you are unsure.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 95, 'Take a different route to work, school, or the store and see how it feels to not know the way.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 96, 'Write down three small things you did well today before you go to sleep.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 97, 'Ask a question you think might be obvious, and notice that nothing bad happens.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 98, 'Offer to make the introduction when two people you know have not met.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 99, 'Apply for something today, a job, a role, a spot on a team, a grant, even if you are not sure you qualify.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 100, 'Try to fix something before you look up how, and give it ten minutes.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 101, 'Ask the person next to you at a checkout, a bus stop, or a waiting room one friendly question.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 102, 'Present one idea at work or in a group with a clear first sentence and no "this is probably silly."'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 103, 'Pick up a musical instrument, a paintbrush, or a pen and make something bad on purpose for ten minutes.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 104, 'Ask for a discount, a better rate, or a price match once today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 105, 'Say what you want for dinner before anyone asks.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 106, 'Tell a story at the table, in a meeting, or in a group chat, start to finish.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 107, 'Write down a time you were wrong and recovered, and what that says about you now.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 108, 'Read aloud to someone, a child, a friend, a pet, for five minutes.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 109, 'Ask a specific person for their advice on a decision you are facing.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 110, 'Take a walk through a neighborhood, park, or building you have never been in.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 111, 'Send the first message in a group that has gone quiet.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 112, 'Say "I disagree" once today, kindly, and give one reason.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 113, 'Do one thing today with your non-dominant hand and laugh at the result.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 114, 'Leave a review for a business you like, with your name on it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 115, 'Choose the unfamiliar item on a menu and order it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 116, 'Keep your hands still and your feet planted while you speak in one conversation.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 117, 'Ask for directions from a stranger instead of your phone.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 118, 'Write down one thing a mentor, coach, or teacher once praised you for and where you still use that skill.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 119, 'Make eye contact with the person serving you and ask how their day is going.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 120, 'Bring one suggestion, not a question, to your next conversation with a manager, teacher, or organizer.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 121, 'Offer to go first when a group is deciding who will.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 122, 'Try a video, a tutorial, or a how-to on a skill you have always assumed was beyond you.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 123, 'Spend five minutes learning the first few phrases of a language you have never studied.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 124, 'Say "thank you for waiting" instead of "sorry I''m late" once today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 125, 'Show up to a place you were nervous about, a gym, a club, a church, a class, and simply be there.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 126, 'Let someone see you make a mistake today and carry on without explaining it away.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 127, 'Text a friend and propose a specific plan with a day and a time.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 128, 'Ask to be included in something, a project, a meeting, an outing, instead of waiting to be asked.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 129, 'Set your own boundary on a phone call: "I have ten minutes, what can I help with?"'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 130, 'Pay a compliment to someone senior to you and let it land.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 131, 'List five small things you handled this week without help.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 132, 'Complete a form, an application, or a registration you have been staring at.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 133, 'Stand at the front of a line, a room, or a class today and look around.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 134, 'Cook or bake something for someone else and hand it over without a disclaimer.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 135, 'Speak to someone in a position of authority today, a manager, a doctor, an official, as an equal.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 136, 'Write down what you are afraid people would think if you tried, then try anyway.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 137, 'Ask a colleague or classmate to swap tasks for an hour so you can try theirs.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 138, 'Give a short toast, a thank you, or a few words at a meal or gathering.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 139, 'Follow up on something you asked for and did not hear back on.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 140, 'Play a game with a stranger, a pickup match, a chess board in a park, an online lobby.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 141, 'Practice a firm handshake or a clear "nice to meet you" with the next new person you meet.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 142, 'Ask for the manager, the supervisor, or the person in charge when you need something resolved.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 143, 'Tell someone about a goal you have, out loud, even if it feels early to say it.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 144, 'Write down one thing you fixed, solved, or figured out this month that you did not think you could.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 145, 'Take the elevator, the bus, or the train alone to somewhere you have not gone by yourself before.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 146, 'Choose the movie, the playlist, or the podcast for the room today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 147, 'Invite a coworker, classmate, or neighbor to lunch, coffee, or a walk.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 148, 'Do a task in front of someone who knows more than you about it and ask them to watch.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 149, 'Say your name clearly, first and last, when you introduce yourself today.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 150, 'Pitch one small change to how something is done at work, at home, or in a group you belong to.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 151, 'Ask someone about a topic you know nothing about and admit you know nothing.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 152, 'Sign your name to something, a card, a letter, a piece of work, a comment, in full.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 153, 'Go into a shop you find intimidating, a high-end store, a specialty shop, a bike shop, and browse.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 154, 'Draft a two-sentence bio for yourself and share it with one person.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 155, 'Hold your position in a discussion for one more sentence than usual before backing down.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 156, 'Try a piece of equipment, a machine, or a tool you have watched other people use and never touched.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 157, 'Enter a raffle, a competition, a contest, or a lottery for a role that you would love to win.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 158, 'Walk into the room, the office, or the party first, ahead of the person you came with.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 159, 'Tell a joke or a funny story to someone today and let the silence be fine if it lands flat.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 160, 'Set up a small stall, a listing, a post, or a sign to sell or give away something you made.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 161, 'Ask for extra time, a different deadline, or a change to a plan that is not working for you.'),
  ('rebuilding-confidence-in-small-steps', 162, 'Practice ordering, asking, or greeting in a language other than your first one, even one word.'),
